const n="tiantiandu-3a",e="8月8日，我们结婚",h="We're Getting Married on August 8",i="中文天天读",t="Reading China",o="3A",s=[{n:1,title:"艾米的信",py:"Àimǐ de xìn",en:"Amy's Letter",chars:303,daodu:"",daoduEn:"",paras:[{zh:"亲爱的爸爸、妈妈：",py:"Qīn'ài de bàba, māma:",en:"Dear Dad and Mom,",fmt:"salute"},{zh:"你们好！",py:"Nǐmen hǎo!",en:"Hello!"},{zh:"你们想我吗？我很想念你们。爸爸的工作一定很忙吧？要多休息。妈妈的身体怎么样？",py:"Nǐmen xiǎng wǒ ma? Wǒ hěn xiǎngniàn nǐmen. Bàba de gōngzuò yídìng hěn máng ba? Yào duō xiūxi. Māma de shēntǐ zěnmeyàng?",en:"Do you miss me? I miss you very much. Dad, you must be very busy at work, right? Make sure you get plenty of rest. Mom, how is your health?"},{zh:"到今天为止，我到中国已经一个月了。我很喜欢这里，因为我交了很多中国朋友，他们很善良也很热情。认识他们我非常高兴。他们给我介绍了很多中国菜。那些菜我都很喜欢，特别是宫保鸡丁和西红柿炒鸡蛋。我也喜欢自己做饭，而且还给我的中国朋友介绍了很多法国菜。他们告诉我，我做的菜很好吃！周末的时候，我们一起去喝酒、唱歌，我还学了一些中文歌。有时我还会跟朋友一起去逛街，我最喜欢买衣服。买完衣服后，我们经常去超市买东西。",py:"Dào jīntiān wéizhǐ, wǒ dào Zhōngguó yǐjīng yí gè yuè le. Wǒ hěn xǐhuan zhèlǐ, yīnwèi wǒ jiāole hěn duō Zhōngguó péngyou, tāmen hěn shànliáng yě hěn rèqíng. Rènshi tāmen wǒ fēicháng gāoxìng. Tāmen gěi wǒ jièshàole hěn duō Zhōngguó cài. Nàxiē cài wǒ dōu hěn xǐhuan, tèbié shì gōngbǎo jīdīng hé xīhóngshì chǎo jīdàn. Wǒ yě xǐhuan zìjǐ zuòfàn, érqiě hái gěi wǒ de Zhōngguó péngyou jièshàole hěn duō Fǎguó cài. Tāmen gàosu wǒ, wǒ zuò de cài hěn hǎochī! Zhōumò de shíhou, wǒmen yìqǐ qù hē jiǔ, chàng gē, wǒ hái xuéle yìxiē Zhōngwén gē. Yǒushí wǒ hái huì gēn péngyou yìqǐ qù guàngjiē, wǒ zuì xǐhuan mǎi yīfu. Mǎiwán yīfu hòu, wǒmen jīngcháng qù chāoshì mǎi dōngxi.",en:"As of today, I have been in China for a month. I really like it here, because I have made lots of Chinese friends. They are very kind and very warm, and I'm so happy to know them. They have introduced me to many Chinese dishes. I like all of them, especially Kung Pao chicken and stir-fried tomatoes with eggs. I also like cooking for myself, and I have introduced lots of French dishes to my Chinese friends. They tell me the food I make is delicious! On weekends we go out drinking and singing together, and I have also learned some Chinese songs. Sometimes I go shopping with friends; buying clothes is my favorite. After buying clothes, we often go to the supermarket to get groceries."},{zh:"最近我的学习很忙，每天下课以后，我都要写汉字、听录音、做练习。因为我们下星期有一个很重要的考试，所以我得好好复习。我觉得学汉语虽然很难，但是很有意思。",py:"Zuìjìn wǒ de xuéxí hěn máng, měi tiān xiàkè yǐhòu, wǒ dōu yào xiě Hànzì, tīng lùyīn, zuò liànxí. Yīnwèi wǒmen xià xīngqī yǒu yí gè hěn zhòngyào de kǎoshì, suǒyǐ wǒ děi hǎohǎo fùxí. Wǒ juéde xué Hànyǔ suīrán hěn nán, dànshì hěn yǒu yìsi.",en:"Lately I've been very busy with my studies. Every day after class I have to write Chinese characters, listen to recordings and do exercises. We have a very important exam next week, so I have to review carefully. I think learning Chinese is hard, but it's very interesting."},{zh:"祝你们健康快乐！",py:"Zhù nǐmen jiànkāng kuàilè!",en:"Wishing you health and happiness!"},{zh:"女儿：艾米",py:"Nǚ'ér: Àimǐ",en:"Your daughter, Amy",fmt:"sign"},{zh:"2008年11月26日",py:"2008 nián 11 yuè 26 rì",en:"November 26, 2008",fmt:"sign"}],vocab:[],points:[],think:[],tf:[],mc:[],tip:null},{n:2,title:"咖啡应该怎么喝？",py:"Kāfēi yīnggāi zěnme hē?",en:"How Should You Drink Coffee?",chars:278,daodu:"",daoduEn:"",paras:[{zh:"很多人都喜欢喝咖啡，特别是年轻人。咖啡里有咖啡因，人喝了会兴奋，身体也会热起来，而且不觉得累。中国的年轻人，现在除了喝茶以外，也越来越喜欢喝咖啡了。关于咖啡还有一句很有名的话：“我不在家，就在咖啡馆；我不在咖啡馆，就在去咖啡馆的路上。”但是，有些人也许不知道喝咖啡应该注意下面这些问题。",py:"Hěn duō rén dōu xǐhuan hē kāfēi, tèbié shì niánqīngrén. Kāfēi li yǒu kāfēiyīn, rén hēle huì xīngfèn, shēntǐ yě huì rè qilai, érqiě bù juéde lèi. Zhōngguó de niánqīngrén, xiànzài chúle hē chá yǐwài, yě yuèláiyuè xǐhuan hē kāfēi le. Guānyú kāfēi hái yǒu yí jù hěn yǒumíng de huà: “Wǒ bú zài jiā, jiù zài kāfēiguǎn; wǒ bú zài kāfēiguǎn, jiù zài qù kāfēiguǎn de lùshang.” Dànshì, yǒuxiē rén yěxǔ bù zhīdào hē kāfēi yīnggāi zhùyì xiàmiàn zhèxiē wèntí.",en:`Many people like drinking coffee, especially young people. Coffee contains caffeine: after drinking it, people feel excited, their bodies warm up, and they don't feel tired. Young people in China now drink tea, and they also like coffee more and more. There's a famous saying about coffee: "If I'm not at home, I'm at the café; if I'm not at the café, I'm on my way to the café." But some people may not know that there are a few things to keep in mind when drinking coffee.`},{zh:"第一，注意时间。饭前不能喝，饭后可以喝。饭前喝咖啡会不想吃东西，但是在饭后喝，对消化很有帮助。另外，咖啡对有胃病的人很不好，它会刺激胃。",py:"Dì-yī, zhùyì shíjiān. Fàn qián bù néng hē, fàn hòu kěyǐ hē. Fàn qián hē kāfēi huì bù xiǎng chī dōngxi, dànshì zài fàn hòu hē, duì xiāohuà hěn yǒu bāngzhù. Lìngwài, kāfēi duì yǒu wèibìng de rén hěn bù hǎo, tā huì cìjī wèi.",en:"First, pay attention to the time. Don't drink it before a meal; you can drink it after a meal. Coffee before a meal will make you not want to eat, but coffee after a meal helps digestion a lot. Also, coffee is very bad for people with stomach problems, because it irritates the stomach."},{zh:"第二，加点儿牛奶。咖啡和牛奶一起喝，可以减少对身体的刺激。比如早饭时喝的咖啡奶，由于其中牛奶比咖啡多，对胃的刺激就小，饭前喝也没问题。",py:"Dì-èr, jiā diǎnr niúnǎi. Kāfēi hé niúnǎi yìqǐ hē, kěyǐ jiǎnshǎo duì shēntǐ de cìjī. Bǐrú zǎofàn shí hē de kāfēinǎi, yóuyú qízhōng niúnǎi bǐ kāfēi duō, duì wèi de cìjī jiù xiǎo, fàn qián hē yě méi wèntí.",en:"Second, add some milk. Drinking coffee with milk makes it less harsh on the body. For example, the milky coffee people drink at breakfast has more milk than coffee in it, so it is gentle on the stomach, and it's fine to drink even before a meal."},{zh:"第三，不要喝太多。一天喝咖啡应该不超过两杯或三杯，否则，太多的咖啡因会让人不舒服。",py:"Dì-sān, búyào hē tài duō. Yì tiān hē kāfēi yīnggāi bù chāoguò liǎng bēi huò sān bēi, fǒuzé, tài duō de kāfēiyīn huì ràng rén bù shūfu.",en:"Third, don't drink too much. You shouldn't drink more than two or three cups of coffee a day; otherwise, too much caffeine will make you feel unwell."}],vocab:[],points:[],think:[],tf:[],mc:[],tip:null},{n:3,title:"给自己的礼物",py:"Gěi zìjǐ de lǐwù",en:"A Gift for Himself",chars:273,daodu:"",daoduEn:"",paras:[{zh:"有个木匠年纪很大了。他告诉老板，自己太老了，想回家跟妻子儿女一起好好生活，不工作了。老板不想让他走，问他可不可以帮忙再盖一座房子。老木匠说可以。但是这次的工作，他没有以前那么认真，盖的房子有很多问题。",py:"Yǒu gè mùjiang niánjì hěn dà le. Tā gàosu lǎobǎn, zìjǐ tài lǎo le, xiǎng huíjiā gēn qīzi érnǚ yìqǐ hǎohǎo shēnghuó, bù gōngzuò le. Lǎobǎn bù xiǎng ràng tā zǒu, wèn tā kě bu kěyǐ bāngmáng zài gài yí zuò fángzi. Lǎo mùjiang shuō kěyǐ. Dànshì zhè cì de gōngzuò, tā méiyǒu yǐqián nàme rènzhēn, gài de fángzi yǒu hěn duō wèntí.",en:"There was a carpenter who had grown very old. He told his boss that he was too old now and wanted to go home and enjoy life with his wife and children, and stop working. The boss didn't want him to leave, and asked if he could help build one more house. The old carpenter said yes. But this time he didn't work as carefully as before, and the house he built had lots of problems."},{zh:"房子盖好后，老板把房子的钥匙给了老木匠，说：“这是你的房子，是我送给你的礼物。”老木匠很吃惊，也很后悔。如果他知道这是给自己盖的房子，他一定会非常认真，用最好的材料，盖最好的房子。可是现在，他只能住在这个质量不好的房子里。",py:"Fángzi gàihǎo hòu, lǎobǎn bǎ fángzi de yàoshi gěile lǎo mùjiang, shuō: “Zhè shì nǐ de fángzi, shì wǒ sòng gěi nǐ de lǐwù.” Lǎo mùjiang hěn chījīng, yě hěn hòuhuǐ. Rúguǒ tā zhīdào zhè shì gěi zìjǐ gài de fángzi, tā yídìng huì fēicháng rènzhēn, yòng zuì hǎo de cáiliào, gài zuì hǎo de fángzi. Kěshì xiànzài, tā zhǐ néng zhù zài zhège zhìliàng bù hǎo de fángzi li.",en:`When the house was finished, the boss gave the keys to the old carpenter and said: "This is your house. It's my gift to you." The old carpenter was very surprised, and full of regret. If he had known he was building the house for himself, he would have been very careful, used the best materials and built the best house. But now he could only live in this poorly built house.`},{zh:"我们每天都在“建造”自己的生活，有时也像这位老木匠，不是每件事都尽了自己最大的努力。我们常常找很多理由来原谅自己在生活中不尽力，原谅自己在工作中不努力。但是，当我们发现问题的时候，可能已经太晚了。",py:"Wǒmen měi tiān dōu zài “jiànzào” zìjǐ de shēnghuó, yǒushí yě xiàng zhè wèi lǎo mùjiang, bú shì měi jiàn shì dōu jìnle zìjǐ zuì dà de nǔlì. Wǒmen chángcháng zhǎo hěn duō lǐyóu lái yuánliàng zìjǐ zài shēnghuó zhōng bú jìnlì, yuánliàng zìjǐ zài gōngzuò zhōng bù nǔlì. Dànshì, dāng wǒmen fāxiàn wèntí de shíhou, kěnéng yǐjīng tài wǎn le.",en:`Every day we are "building" our own lives, and sometimes we are like this old carpenter: we don't give our very best to everything. We often find lots of excuses to forgive ourselves for not trying our best in life and not working hard at our jobs. But by the time we notice the problems, it may already be too late.`}],vocab:[],points:[],think:[],tf:[],mc:[],tip:null},{n:4,title:"“请慢用”和“以后再说”",py:"“Qǐng màn yòng” hé “yǐhòu zài shuō”",en:`"Enjoy Your Meal" and "Let's Talk Later"`,chars:363,daodu:"",daoduEn:"",paras:[{zh:"一来中国，我就认识了很多中国朋友。一天中午下课，我遇到一个中国同学。她问我：“吃了吗？”我想她一定是想和我一起吃饭，就马上说：“没有呢，我们一起去吧。”",py:"Yì lái Zhōngguó, wǒ jiù rènshile hěn duō Zhōngguó péngyou. Yì tiān zhōngwǔ xiàkè, wǒ yùdào yí gè Zhōngguó tóngxué. Tā wèn wǒ: “Chīle ma?” Wǒ xiǎng tā yídìng shì xiǎng hé wǒ yìqǐ chīfàn, jiù mǎshàng shuō: “Méiyǒu ne, wǒmen yìqǐ qù ba.”",en:`As soon as I came to China, I got to know lots of Chinese friends. One day at noon after class, I ran into a Chinese classmate. She asked me: "Have you eaten?" I thought she must want to have lunch with me, so I said right away: "Not yet. Let's go together."`},{zh:"她好像有点儿吃惊，但还是和我去了学校旁边的小饭馆。服务员上菜说：“这是你们点的宫保鸡丁，请慢用。”",py:"Tā hǎoxiàng yǒudiǎnr chījīng, dàn háishi hé wǒ qùle xuéxiào pángbiān de xiǎo fànguǎn. Fúwùyuán shàng cài shuō: “Zhè shì nǐmen diǎn de gōngbǎo jīdīng, qǐng màn yòng.”",en:`She seemed a little surprised, but she still went with me to the small restaurant next to the school. The waiter brought the dish and said: "Here's the Kung Pao chicken you ordered. Qǐng màn yòng."`},{zh:"我不明白“请慢用”是什么意思。中国朋友说，就是“请你慢慢吃”的意思。我更奇怪了，我吃饭不快啊，为什么服务员让我“慢慢吃”？",py:"Wǒ bù míngbai “qǐng màn yòng” shì shénme yìsi. Zhōngguó péngyou shuō, jiù shì “qǐng nǐ mànmàn chī” de yìsi. Wǒ gèng qíguài le, wǒ chīfàn bú kuài a, wèi shénme fúwùyuán ràng wǒ “mànmàn chī”?",en:`I didn't understand what "qǐng màn yòng" meant. My Chinese friend said it means "please eat slowly." That puzzled me even more. I don't eat fast! Why did the waiter tell me to "eat slowly"? (It is really a polite way to say "Enjoy your meal.")`},{zh:"吃完饭，中国朋友叫服务员结账。我知道该付钱了，就拿出钱准备付我那一半。没想到中国朋友急忙说：“今天我请客！”",py:"Chīwán fàn, Zhōngguó péngyou jiào fúwùyuán jiézhàng. Wǒ zhīdào gāi fù qián le, jiù náchū qián zhǔnbèi fù wǒ nà yíbàn. Méi xiǎngdào Zhōngguó péngyou jímáng shuō: “Jīntiān wǒ qǐngkè!”",en:`After the meal, my Chinese friend called the waiter for the bill. I knew it was time to pay, so I took out some money to pay my half. To my surprise, my Chinese friend said quickly: "It's my treat today!"`},{zh:"很久以后我才明白，中国人觉得吃完饭大家都拿出钱来，自己付自己的很没意思。他们喜欢这样：这次你花钱请客，下次我来付钱，第三次还是你，第四次又是我……",py:"Hěn jiǔ yǐhòu wǒ cái míngbai, Zhōngguórén juéde chīwán fàn dàjiā dōu náchū qián lái, zìjǐ fù zìjǐ de hěn méi yìsi. Tāmen xǐhuan zhèyàng: zhè cì nǐ huā qián qǐngkè, xià cì wǒ lái fù qián, dì-sān cì háishi nǐ, dì-sì cì yòu shì wǒ...",en:"Only much later did I understand: Chinese people feel that when everyone takes out money after a meal and each pays for themselves, it's no fun. They like it this way: this time you treat, next time I pay, the third time it's you again, the fourth time it's me again..."},{zh:"有一天，我跟一个中国朋友打电话聊天。我高兴地跟她聊起我去长城的事情，说了差不多半个小时。快挂电话时，她说：“等你以后有时间，欢迎你来我家玩儿。”",py:"Yǒu yì tiān, wǒ gēn yí gè Zhōngguó péngyou dǎ diànhuà liáotiān. Wǒ gāoxìng de gēn tā liáoqǐ wǒ qù Chángchéng de shìqing, shuōle chàbuduō bàn gè xiǎoshí. Kuài guà diànhuà shí, tā shuō: “Děng nǐ yǐhòu yǒu shíjiān, huānyíng nǐ lái wǒ jiā wánr.”",en:`One day I was chatting on the phone with a Chinese friend. I happily told her about my trip to the Great Wall and talked for almost half an hour. Just before we hung up, she said: "When you have time someday, you're welcome to come over to my place."`},{zh:"那时我已经到中国半年了，我知道她的意思是“再见”，所以我也很“中国”地说：“好，谢谢，以后再说吧。”",py:"Nà shí wǒ yǐjīng dào Zhōngguó bàn nián le, wǒ zhīdào tā de yìsi shì “zàijiàn”, suǒyǐ wǒ yě hěn “Zhōngguó” de shuō: “Hǎo, xièxie, yǐhòu zài shuō ba.”",en:`By then I had been in China for half a year, and I knew she just meant "goodbye." So I answered in a very "Chinese" way: "OK, thanks. Let's talk about it later."`}],vocab:[],points:[],think:[],tf:[],mc:[],tip:null},{n:5,title:"北方和南方",py:"Běifāng hé nánfāng",en:"North and South",chars:277,daodu:"",daoduEn:"",paras:[{zh:"今年一月，我从上海来到了北京，慢慢发现了中国南北方的很多差别。",py:"Jīnnián yī yuè, wǒ cóng Shànghǎi láidàole Běijīng, mànmàn fāxiànle Zhōngguó nánběifāng de hěn duō chābié.",en:"This January I came from Shanghai to Beijing, and little by little I discovered many differences between northern and southern China."},{zh:"先说气候。北方比较干燥，南方比较潮湿。每年一月，最北边的黑龙江省气温很低，大概零下30摄氏度（-30℃），人们出门的时候要穿上厚厚的衣服。最南边的海南省却非常暖和，人们都穿着夏天的衣服，还可以在海里游泳。",py:"Xiān shuō qìhòu. Běifāng bǐjiào gānzào, nánfāng bǐjiào cháoshī. Měi nián yī yuè, zuì běibian de Hēilóngjiāng Shěng qìwēn hěn dī, dàgài língxià 30 shèshìdù (-30℃), rénmen chūmén de shíhou yào chuānshang hòuhòu de yīfu. Zuì nánbian de Hǎinán Shěng què fēicháng nuǎnhuo, rénmen dōu chuānzhe xiàtiān de yīfu, hái kěyǐ zài hǎi li yóuyǒng.",en:"First, the climate. The north is rather dry, and the south is rather humid. Every January, in Heilongjiang Province in the far north, the temperature is very low, about minus 30 degrees Celsius (-30℃), and people have to put on thick clothes when they go out. But Hainan Province in the far south is very warm: people wear summer clothes and can even swim in the sea."},{zh:"北方菜和南方菜也不一样。北方人喜欢咸一点儿的，南方人喜欢吃甜的，大多数北方人爱吃面食，而很多南方人却喜欢吃米饭。",py:"Běifāng cài hé nánfāng cài yě bù yíyàng. Běifāngrén xǐhuan xián yìdiǎnr de, nánfāngrén xǐhuan chī tián de, dàduōshù běifāngrén ài chī miànshí, ér hěn duō nánfāngrén què xǐhuan chī mǐfàn.",en:"Northern and southern food are different too. Northerners like their food a bit salty, while southerners like sweet food. Most northerners love wheat foods such as noodles and buns, while many southerners prefer rice."},{zh:"让人想不到的是，南方人和北方人问路也不同。北方人，特别是北京人，常说“东、西、南、北”，而南方人却喜欢说“前、后、左、右”。从上海到北京的那天，下车以后，我用汉语问路，有人对我说：“往东走！”可是我刚到北京，对这里很不熟悉，不知道哪儿是东，哪儿是南。所以，我根本不知道“往东走”是往哪儿走。",py:"Ràng rén xiǎngbudào de shì, nánfāngrén hé běifāngrén wèn lù yě bùtóng. Běifāngrén, tèbié shì Běijīngrén, cháng shuō “dōng, xī, nán, běi”, ér nánfāngrén què xǐhuan shuō “qián, hòu, zuǒ, yòu”. Cóng Shànghǎi dào Běijīng de nà tiān, xià chē yǐhòu, wǒ yòng Hànyǔ wèn lù, yǒu rén duì wǒ shuō: “Wǎng dōng zǒu!” Kěshì wǒ gāng dào Běijīng, duì zhèlǐ hěn bù shúxī, bù zhīdào nǎr shì dōng, nǎr shì nán. Suǒyǐ, wǒ gēnběn bù zhīdào “wǎng dōng zǒu” shì wǎng nǎr zǒu.",en:`Surprisingly, southerners and northerners even ask for directions differently. Northerners, especially people in Beijing, often say "east, west, south, north," while southerners prefer "front, back, left, right." On the day I came from Shanghai to Beijing, I got off the train and asked for directions in Chinese. Someone told me: "Go east!" But I had just arrived in Beijing and didn't know the place at all. I didn't know which way was east or which way was south. So I had no idea which way "go east" meant.`}],vocab:[],points:[],think:[],tf:[],mc:[],tip:null},{n:6,title:"公园的早晨",py:"Gōngyuán de zǎochen",en:"Morning in the Park",chars:327,daodu:"",daoduEn:"",paras:[{zh:"北京有大大小小的公园两百多个，这些公园无论大小，开门都很早。每天都会有很多游客去公园，但是最早的客人却都是住在附近晨练的人。很多中国人，特别是中老年人，不仅喜欢晨练，而且坚持每天晨练。",py:"Běijīng yǒu dàdàxiǎoxiǎo de gōngyuán liǎngbǎi duō gè, zhèxiē gōngyuán wúlùn dàxiǎo, kāimén dōu hěn zǎo. Měi tiān dōu huì yǒu hěn duō yóukè qù gōngyuán, dànshì zuì zǎo de kèrén què dōu shì zhù zài fùjìn chénliàn de rén. Hěn duō Zhōngguórén, tèbié shì zhōng-lǎoniánrén, bùjǐn xǐhuan chénliàn, érqiě jiānchí měi tiān chénliàn.",en:"Beijing has more than two hundred parks, big and small, and no matter their size, they all open very early. Lots of visitors go to the parks every day, but the earliest guests are always people who live nearby and come for morning exercise. Many Chinese people, especially the middle-aged and elderly, not only like morning exercise but do it every single day."},{zh:"人们开始晨练的时间不太一样。最早的五点就开始，而大多数人是六点到七点。这个时候你去公园，会看到很多人在做各种各样的运动。喜欢安静的人可以打太极拳，喜欢热闹的人可以听着音乐做操、跳舞，一个人可以散步、慢跑，两三个人可以打羽毛球、打网球，很多老人在公园里唱歌、唱京剧，还有人用很长的大毛笔在地上写字。",py:"Rénmen kāishǐ chénliàn de shíjiān bú tài yíyàng. Zuì zǎo de wǔ diǎn jiù kāishǐ, ér dàduōshù rén shì liù diǎn dào qī diǎn. Zhège shíhou nǐ qù gōngyuán, huì kàndào hěn duō rén zài zuò gèzhǒng gèyàng de yùndòng. Xǐhuan ānjìng de rén kěyǐ dǎ tàijíquán, xǐhuan rènao de rén kěyǐ tīngzhe yīnyuè zuò cāo, tiàowǔ, yí gè rén kěyǐ sànbù, mànpǎo, liǎng-sān gè rén kěyǐ dǎ yǔmáoqiú, dǎ wǎngqiú, hěn duō lǎorén zài gōngyuán li chàng gē, chàng jīngjù, hái yǒu rén yòng hěn cháng de dà máobǐ zài dìshang xiě zì.",en:"People start their morning exercise at different times. The earliest begin at five o'clock, but most people come between six and seven. If you go to a park at this time, you'll see lots of people doing all kinds of exercise. People who like quiet can do tai chi; people who like a lively crowd can do exercises or dance to music. One person can take a walk or jog; two or three people can play badminton or tennis. Many old people sing songs or Peking Opera in the park, and some people even write characters on the ground with a very long, big brush."},{zh:"晨练是不是真的对身体有好处，不同的人有不同的看法。有的人觉得早晨的空气很新鲜，也有人认为早上的空气不太好，最好的运动时间是下午四点到六点。不过大多数中国人还是习惯早上运动，他们相信“早睡早起身体好”，相信在运动以后，可以轻轻松松地开始新的一天。",py:"Chénliàn shì bu shì zhēn de duì shēntǐ yǒu hǎochù, bùtóng de rén yǒu bùtóng de kànfǎ. Yǒude rén juéde zǎochen de kōngqì hěn xīnxiān, yě yǒu rén rènwéi zǎoshang de kōngqì bú tài hǎo, zuì hǎo de yùndòng shíjiān shì xiàwǔ sì diǎn dào liù diǎn. Búguò dàduōshù Zhōngguórén háishi xíguàn zǎoshang yùndòng, tāmen xiāngxìn “zǎo shuì zǎo qǐ shēntǐ hǎo”, xiāngxìn zài yùndòng yǐhòu, kěyǐ qīngqīngsōngsōng de kāishǐ xīn de yì tiān.",en:`Is morning exercise really good for your health? Different people have different opinions. Some think the morning air is very fresh; others think the morning air isn't very good, and that the best time to exercise is from four to six in the afternoon. Still, most Chinese people are used to exercising in the morning. They believe "early to bed and early to rise keeps you healthy," and that after exercising they can start a new day feeling relaxed.`}],vocab:[],points:[],think:[],tf:[],mc:[],tip:null},{n:7,title:"别告诉我该做什么",py:"Bié gàosu wǒ gāi zuò shénme",en:"Don't Tell Me What to Do",chars:350,daodu:"",daoduEn:"",paras:[{zh:"有位外国妈妈每次带她的孩子出去，都会在路上遇到中国邻居。她们总是会停下来，看看她的孩子，微笑着说：“这孩子真漂亮！真可爱！孩子多大了？你每天都带他出来散步吗？”",py:"Yǒu wèi wàiguó māma měi cì dài tā de háizi chūqù, dōu huì zài lùshang yùdào Zhōngguó línjū. Tāmen zǒngshì huì tíng xialai, kànkan tā de háizi, wēixiàozhe shuō: “Zhè háizi zhēn piàoliang! Zhēn kě'ài! Háizi duō dà le? Nǐ měi tiān dōu dài tā chūlai sànbù ma?”",en:'There was a foreign mother who, every time she took her child out, ran into her Chinese neighbors on the street. They would always stop, look at her child and say with a smile: "What a beautiful baby! So cute! How old is the baby? Do you bring him out for a walk every day?"'},{zh:"开始的时候，这位妈妈很高兴，也愿意回答这些问题。",py:"Kāishǐ de shíhou, zhè wèi māma hěn gāoxìng, yě yuànyì huídá zhèxiē wèntí.",en:"At first, the mother was very happy and was glad to answer these questions."},{zh:"可是，问题却越来越多了。人们开始问：“这孩子像你，还是像他爸爸？”“孩子每天吃什么？”后来，很多中国妈妈非常认真地告诉她：“这么冷的天你不能只给孩子穿袜子，一定要穿上鞋！”特别是一些年纪大的妈妈或者奶奶还会说：“如果你不给孩子穿鞋，孩子一定会生病的！”",py:"Kěshì, wèntí què yuèláiyuè duō le. Rénmen kāishǐ wèn: “Zhè háizi xiàng nǐ, háishi xiàng tā bàba?” “Háizi měi tiān chī shénme?” Hòulái, hěn duō Zhōngguó māma fēicháng rènzhēn de gàosu tā: “Zhème lěng de tiān nǐ bù néng zhǐ gěi háizi chuān wàzi, yídìng yào chuānshang xié!” Tèbié shì yìxiē niánjì dà de māma huòzhě nǎinai hái huì shuō: “Rúguǒ nǐ bù gěi háizi chuān xié, háizi yídìng huì shēngbìng de!”",en:`But there were more and more questions. People started asking: "Does the baby look like you or like his dad?" "What does the baby eat every day?" Later, many Chinese mothers told her very seriously: "On such a cold day you can't just put socks on the baby. He must wear shoes!" Some older mothers and grandmothers would even say: "If you don't put shoes on the baby, the baby will surely get sick!"`},{zh:"当第十个人这样说的时候，外国妈妈终于有点儿生气了。她问自己的中国朋友：“我是孩子的妈妈，这是我的孩子。她们为什么要告诉我该怎么做？”",py:"Dāng dì-shí gè rén zhèyàng shuō de shíhou, wàiguó māma zhōngyú yǒudiǎnr shēngqì le. Tā wèn zìjǐ de Zhōngguó péngyou: “Wǒ shì háizi de māma, zhè shì wǒ de háizi. Tāmen wèi shénme yào gàosu wǒ gāi zěnme zuò?”",en:`When the tenth person said this, the foreign mother finally got a little angry. She asked her Chinese friend: "I'm the child's mother, and this is my child. Why do they keep telling me what to do?"`},{zh:"她的中国朋友赶忙告诉她：“这些人可能觉得，这里的天气又干又冷，你还不太了解。而且，对中国妈妈们来说，把自己照顾孩子的经验告诉年轻的妈妈，是应该做的，也是一定要做的。特别是年纪大的女性，更觉得帮助年轻的妈妈是自己的责任。”",py:"Tā de Zhōngguó péngyou gǎnmáng gàosu tā: “Zhèxiē rén kěnéng juéde, zhèlǐ de tiānqì yòu gān yòu lěng, nǐ hái bú tài liǎojiě. Érqiě, duì Zhōngguó māmamen lái shuō, bǎ zìjǐ zhàogù háizi de jīngyàn gàosu niánqīng de māma, shì yīnggāi zuò de, yě shì yídìng yào zuò de. Tèbié shì niánjì dà de nǚxìng, gèng juéde bāngzhù niánqīng de māma shì zìjǐ de zérèn.”",en:`Her Chinese friend quickly told her: "These people probably think the weather here is dry and cold, and you don't know it well yet. Besides, for Chinese mothers, passing on their experience of caring for children to young mothers is something they should do, even something they must do. Older women especially feel that helping young mothers is their duty."`}],vocab:[],points:[],think:[],tf:[],mc:[],tip:null},{n:8,title:"中国美食——火锅",py:"Zhōngguó měishí — huǒguō",en:"Chinese Food: Hot Pot",chars:286,daodu:"",daoduEn:"",paras:[{zh:"火锅是中国最常见的美食之一，中国的很多城市都有火锅店。秋天和冬天吃火锅最好。天气越冷，火锅店的生意越红火。",py:"Huǒguō shì Zhōngguó zuì chángjiàn de měishí zhī yī, Zhōngguó de hěn duō chéngshì dōu yǒu huǒguōdiàn. Qiūtiān hé dōngtiān chī huǒguō zuì hǎo. Tiānqì yuè lěng, huǒguōdiàn de shēngyi yuè hónghuo.",en:"Hot pot is one of the most common dishes in China, and many Chinese cities have hot pot restaurants. Autumn and winter are the best seasons for hot pot. The colder the weather, the better business is at hot pot restaurants."},{zh:"人们喜欢火锅的原因很多。",py:"Rénmen xǐhuan huǒguō de yuányīn hěn duō.",en:"There are many reasons why people like hot pot."},{zh:"第一，火锅种类多，既有传统火锅，也有多种新式火锅，例如鱼头火锅、菊花火锅、四季火锅等等，满足了顾客的各种口味。",py:"Dì-yī, huǒguō zhǒnglèi duō, jì yǒu chuántǒng huǒguō, yě yǒu duō zhǒng xīnshì huǒguō, lìrú yútóu huǒguō, júhuā huǒguō, sìjì huǒguō děngděng, mǎnzúle gùkè de gè zhǒng kǒuwèi.",en:"First, there are many kinds of hot pot. There is traditional hot pot, and there are many new styles too, such as fish-head hot pot, chrysanthemum hot pot and four-season hot pot, which suit all kinds of customers' tastes."},{zh:"第二，火锅原料多种多样，肉、鱼、虾、蔬菜、豆腐等，都可以做火锅原料。这样，你可以一次吃到几十种不同食物。",py:"Dì-èr, huǒguō yuánliào duōzhǒng duōyàng, ròu, yú, xiā, shūcài, dòufu děng, dōu kěyǐ zuò huǒguō yuánliào. Zhèyàng, nǐ kěyǐ yí cì chīdào jǐshí zhǒng bùtóng shíwù.",en:"Second, hot pot ingredients are many and varied: meat, fish, shrimp, vegetables, tofu and more can all go into a hot pot. This way, you can eat dozens of different foods at one meal."},{zh:"第三，火锅的做法很简单，把原料放到锅里涮一涮，熟了就能吃了。",py:"Dì-sān, huǒguō de zuòfǎ hěn jiǎndān, bǎ yuánliào fàngdào guō li shuàn yi shuàn, shú le jiù néng chī le.",en:"Third, hot pot is very easy to cook: put the ingredients into the pot, swish them around a little, and once they're cooked you can eat."},{zh:"第四，也是最重要的一个原因——火锅非常适合朋友们一起吃。大家坐在火锅旁边，选择自己爱吃的食物，边吃边聊，非常随意，交流也更加方便。",py:"Dì-sì, yě shì zuì zhòngyào de yí gè yuányīn — huǒguō fēicháng shìhé péngyoumen yìqǐ chī. Dàjiā zuò zài huǒguō pángbiān, xuǎnzé zìjǐ ài chī de shíwù, biān chī biān liáo, fēicháng suíyì, jiāoliú yě gèngjiā fāngbiàn.",en:"Fourth, and the most important reason: hot pot is perfect for eating with friends. Everyone sits around the hot pot, picks the foods they like, and eats and chats at the same time. It's very relaxed, and it's easier to talk with each other."},{zh:"火锅虽然非常好吃，但在吃火锅时有两点需要注意：一要注意原料新鲜，二要注意涮的时间，食物在锅里涮的时间既不能太长，也不能太短。",py:"Huǒguō suīrán fēicháng hǎochī, dàn zài chī huǒguō shí yǒu liǎng diǎn xūyào zhùyì: yī yào zhùyì yuánliào xīnxiān, èr yào zhùyì shuàn de shíjiān, shíwù zài guō li shuàn de shíjiān jì bù néng tài cháng, yě bù néng tài duǎn.",en:"Hot pot is delicious, but there are two things to watch out for when you eat it: first, make sure the ingredients are fresh; second, watch the cooking time. Food should stay in the pot neither too long nor too short."}],vocab:[],points:[],think:[],tf:[],mc:[],tip:null},{n:9,title:"三个不同的选择",py:"Sān gè bùtóng de xuǎnzé",en:"Three Different Choices",chars:253,daodu:"",daoduEn:"",paras:[{zh:"有ABC三个人要被关进监狱三年，监狱长允许他们一人提一个要求。",py:"Yǒu ABC sān gè rén yào bèi guānjìn jiānyù sān nián, jiānyùzhǎng yǔnxǔ tāmen yì rén tí yí gè yāoqiú.",en:"Three men, A, B and C, were going to be locked up in prison for three years. The prison warden allowed each of them to make one request."},{zh:"A爱抽烟，要了三箱烟。",py:"A ài chōuyān, yàole sān xiāng yān.",en:"A loved smoking, so he asked for three boxes of cigarettes."},{zh:"B最浪漫，要一个美丽的女子和他一起生活。",py:"B zuì làngmàn, yào yí gè měilì de nǚzǐ hé tā yìqǐ shēnghuó.",en:"B was the most romantic. He asked for a beautiful woman to live with him."},{zh:"而C说，他要一部与外面联系的电话。",py:"Ér C shuō, tā yào yí bù yǔ wàimiàn liánxì de diànhuà.",en:"And C said he wanted a telephone to keep in touch with the outside world."},{zh:"三年过后，第一个跑出来的是A。他嘴里、鼻孔里塞满了烟，一出来就大喊道：“给我火，给我火！”原来他忘了要火了。",py:"Sān nián guòhòu, dì-yī gè pǎo chulai de shì A. Tā zuǐ li, bíkǒng li sāimǎnle yān, yì chūlai jiù dà hǎn dào: “Gěi wǒ huǒ, gěi wǒ huǒ!” Yuánlái tā wàngle yào huǒ le.",en:'Three years later, the first to run out was A. His mouth and nostrils were stuffed with cigarettes, and as soon as he came out he shouted: "Give me a light! Give me a light!" It turned out he had forgotten to ask for something to light them with.'},{zh:"接着出来的是B。只见他手里抱着一个小孩子，美丽的女子手里牵着一个小孩子，而在她肚子里还有他们的第三个孩子。",py:"Jiēzhe chūlai de shì B. Zhǐ jiàn tā shǒu li bàozhe yí gè xiǎo háizi, měilì de nǚzǐ shǒu li qiānzhe yí gè xiǎo háizi, ér zài tā dùzi li hái yǒu tāmen de dì-sān gè háizi.",en:"Next came B. He was carrying a small child in his arms, the beautiful woman was leading another small child by the hand, and in her belly was their third child."},{zh:"最后出来的是C。他紧紧握住监狱长的手说：“这三年来我每天与外面联系，我的生意不但没有停下来，反而增长了200%。我一定要送你一辆汽车！”",py:"Zuìhòu chūlai de shì C. Tā jǐnjǐn wòzhù jiānyùzhǎng de shǒu shuō: “Zhè sān nián lái wǒ měi tiān yǔ wàimiàn liánxì, wǒ de shēngyi búdàn méiyǒu tíng xialai, fǎn'ér zēngzhǎngle 200%. Wǒ yídìng yào sòng nǐ yí liàng qìchē!”",en:`The last to come out was C. He shook the warden's hand firmly and said: "For these three years I've been in touch with the outside world every day. My business didn't stop. In fact, it grew by 200%. I must give you a car!"`},{zh:"这个故事告诉我们，ABC三个人今天的生活是他们三年前的选择决定的。什么样的选择决定什么样的生活。",py:"Zhège gùshi gàosu wǒmen, ABC sān gè rén jīntiān de shēnghuó shì tāmen sān nián qián de xuǎnzé juédìng de. Shénmeyàng de xuǎnzé juédìng shénmeyàng de shēnghuó.",en:"This story tells us that the lives A, B and C have today were decided by the choices they made three years ago. The choices you make decide the life you will have."}],vocab:[],points:[],think:[],tf:[],mc:[],tip:null},{n:10,title:"中国人怎么买车？",py:"Zhōngguórén zěnme mǎi chē?",en:"How Do Chinese People Buy Cars?",chars:260,daodu:"",daoduEn:"",paras:[{zh:"星期六早上走进汽车销售公司，一边吃着免费的汉堡，一边看车、听介绍，不一会儿，付钱、拿车钥匙、开车回家——这是美国人在买车。",py:"Xīngqīliù zǎoshang zǒujìn qìchē xiāoshòu gōngsī, yìbiān chīzhe miǎnfèi de hànbǎo, yìbiān kàn chē, tīng jièshào, bù yíhuìr, fù qián, ná chē yàoshi, kāichē huíjiā — zhè shì Měiguórén zài mǎi chē.",en:"Walk into a car dealership on Saturday morning, look at cars and listen to the salesperson while eating a free hamburger, and before long, pay, take the keys and drive home. That's how Americans buy a car."},{zh:"慢慢走到汽车销售公司，告诉他们自己想要什么车，然后回家，等几个星期，自己买的车才能送到。虽然慢，可这一定是“自己的车”，和别人的车不一样——这是欧洲人在买车。",py:"Mànmàn zǒudào qìchē xiāoshòu gōngsī, gàosu tāmen zìjǐ xiǎng yào shénme chē, ránhòu huíjiā, děng jǐ gè xīngqī, zìjǐ mǎi de chē cái néng sòngdào. Suīrán màn, kě zhè yídìng shì “zìjǐ de chē”, hé biérén de chē bù yíyàng — zhè shì Ōuzhōurén zài mǎi chē.",en:`Stroll to a car dealership, tell them what kind of car you want, then go home and wait a few weeks before your car is delivered. It's slow, but it's sure to be "your own car," different from everyone else's. That's how Europeans buy a car.`},{zh:"那么中国人呢？有人说，中国人买车像读MBA，要找很多资料，还要经常“做作业”：每种车多少钱？哪国的？有什么特点？如果以后车坏了，修车方便不方便？还有最重要的，每千米要用多少油？最后，拿着几种自己最满意的车的资料，去销售公司试车。中国人很少一个人看车买车，而是全家都去。虽然太太可能不懂车，孩子可能也不懂车，但也要一起去看，最后一起决定。",py:"Nàme Zhōngguórén ne? Yǒu rén shuō, Zhōngguórén mǎi chē xiàng dú MBA, yào zhǎo hěn duō zīliào, hái yào jīngcháng “zuò zuòyè”: měi zhǒng chē duōshao qián? Nǎ guó de? Yǒu shénme tèdiǎn? Rúguǒ yǐhòu chē huài le, xiū chē fāngbiàn bu fāngbiàn? Hái yǒu zuì zhòngyào de, měi qiānmǐ yào yòng duōshao yóu? Zuìhòu, názhe jǐ zhǒng zìjǐ zuì mǎnyì de chē de zīliào, qù xiāoshòu gōngsī shì chē. Zhōngguórén hěn shǎo yí gè rén kàn chē mǎi chē, ér shì quán jiā dōu qù. Suīrán tàitai kěnéng bù dǒng chē, háizi kěnéng yě bù dǒng chē, dàn yě yào yìqǐ qù kàn, zuìhòu yìqǐ juédìng.",en:`And the Chinese? Some say buying a car in China is like studying for an MBA. You have to gather lots of information and keep "doing homework": How much does each car cost? Which country is it from? What's special about it? If it breaks down later, is it easy to get it repaired? And most important of all, how much fuel does it use per kilometer? Finally, with information on the few cars they like best, they go to the dealership for a test drive. Chinese people rarely go car shopping alone; the whole family goes. The wife may know nothing about cars, and neither may the child, but they all go to look together and make the final decision together.`}],vocab:[],points:[],think:[],tf:[],mc:[],tip:null},{n:11,title:"打招呼也不同",py:"Dǎ zhāohu yě bùtóng",en:"Greetings Are Different Too",chars:303,daodu:"",daoduEn:"",paras:[{zh:"我叫玛丽，是美国人，我来中国一年了。刚到中国时，我像在美国一样，遇到不认识的人也笑着打招呼。如果在街上，我说“Hi”，如果在学校里，我说“Hello”。但是，我发现，我的做法有时候会让中国人吓一跳！比如，我在校园里遇到中国同学，就先笑着问候他们。但是，他们看到我的笑容都有点儿吃惊。有的人也会笑着点头，还有些人虽然听到了，却没反应。",py:"Wǒ jiào Mǎlì, shì Měiguórén, wǒ lái Zhōngguó yì nián le. Gāng dào Zhōngguó shí, wǒ xiàng zài Měiguó yíyàng, yùdào bú rènshi de rén yě xiàozhe dǎ zhāohu. Rúguǒ zài jiē shang, wǒ shuō “Hi”, rúguǒ zài xuéxiào li, wǒ shuō “Hello”. Dànshì, wǒ fāxiàn, wǒ de zuòfǎ yǒu shíhou huì ràng Zhōngguórén xià yí tiào! Bǐrú, wǒ zài xiàoyuán li yùdào Zhōngguó tóngxué, jiù xiān xiàozhe wènhòu tāmen. Dànshì, tāmen kàndào wǒ de xiàoróng dōu yǒudiǎnr chījīng. Yǒude rén yě huì xiàozhe diǎntóu, hái yǒuxiē rén suīrán tīngdào le, què méi fǎnyìng.",en:`My name is Mary. I'm American, and I've been in China for a year. When I first arrived, I did just what I did in America: I smiled and said hello even to people I didn't know. On the street I'd say "Hi," and at school I'd say "Hello." But I found that this sometimes startled Chinese people! For example, when I met Chinese students on campus, I'd smile and greet them first. But they all looked a little surprised at my smile. Some smiled and nodded back, while others heard me but didn't react.`},{zh:"为什么呢？我觉得很奇怪。看来，我还不太了解中国人。",py:"Wèi shénme ne? Wǒ juéde hěn qíguài. Kànlái, wǒ hái bú tài liǎojiě Zhōngguórén.",en:"Why? I found it very strange. It seemed I still didn't understand Chinese people very well."},{zh:"我的法国同屋告诉我：“中国人对认识的人微笑比较多，对不认识的人微笑比较少。我刚来的时候，也没有中国同学主动跟我打招呼。但现在我们熟悉了，在图书馆、食堂遇到了，他们都会笑着跟我打招呼。”",py:"Wǒ de Fǎguó tóngwū gàosu wǒ: “Zhōngguórén duì rènshi de rén wēixiào bǐjiào duō, duì bú rènshi de rén wēixiào bǐjiào shǎo. Wǒ gāng lái de shíhou, yě méiyǒu Zhōngguó tóngxué zhǔdòng gēn wǒ dǎ zhāohu. Dàn xiànzài wǒmen shúxī le, zài túshūguǎn, shítáng yùdào le, tāmen dōu huì xiàozhe gēn wǒ dǎ zhāohu.”",en:`My French roommate told me: "Chinese people smile a lot at people they know, but not much at people they don't know. When I first came, no Chinese students said hello to me first either. But now we know each other, and when we meet in the library or the dining hall, they always smile and say hello."`},{zh:"听完她的话，我才知道中国人是怎么打招呼的：他们不习惯跟不认识的人打招呼，大多数中国人只是在有事的时候才跟不认识的人打招呼。亲爱的朋友，我说得对吗？",py:"Tīngwán tā de huà, wǒ cái zhīdào Zhōngguórén shì zěnme dǎ zhāohu de: tāmen bù xíguàn gēn bú rènshi de rén dǎ zhāohu, dàduōshù Zhōngguórén zhǐshì zài yǒu shì de shíhou cái gēn bú rènshi de rén dǎ zhāohu. Qīn'ài de péngyou, wǒ shuō de duì ma?",en:"After hearing this, I finally understood how Chinese people greet each other: they aren't used to greeting strangers, and most Chinese people only speak to strangers when they need something. Dear friends, am I right?"}],vocab:[],points:[],think:[],tf:[],mc:[],tip:null},{n:12,title:"中国的高考——考全家",py:"Zhōngguó de gāokǎo — kǎo quán jiā",en:"China's College Entrance Exam: A Test for the Whole Family",chars:323,daodu:"",daoduEn:"",paras:[{zh:"2007年6月7日，高考第一天，全国有1000多万高三学生走进了考场。他们中最后能上大学的只有570万左右。",py:"2007 nián 6 yuè 7 rì, gāokǎo dì-yī tiān, quánguó yǒu 1000 duō wàn gāosān xuéshēng zǒujìnle kǎochǎng. Tāmen zhōng zuìhòu néng shàng dàxué de zhǐyǒu 570 wàn zuǒyòu.",en:"On June 7, 2007, the first day of the gaokao (the national college entrance exam), more than 10 million high school seniors across the country walked into the exam halls. In the end, only about 5.7 million of them would get into university."},{zh:"很多父母这一天都请假不上班，一家三口人都来到考场。一些学生的家比较远，父母还给他们预订了考场附近的宾馆。",py:"Hěn duō fùmǔ zhè yì tiān dōu qǐngjià bú shàngbān, yì jiā sān kǒu rén dōu láidào kǎochǎng. Yìxiē xuéshēng de jiā bǐjiào yuǎn, fùmǔ hái gěi tāmen yùdìngle kǎochǎng fùjìn de bīnguǎn.",en:"On this day many parents take time off work, and whole families of three come to the exam site. Some students live rather far away, so their parents even book hotels near the exam site for them."},{zh:"早上九点，考试开始。有的父母马上回家给孩子准备午饭，更多的父母会留在考场外面等孩子。虽然不少父母工作忙，很难请假，但是他们都觉得高考和结婚、生孩子一样，是一生只有一次的大事，所以这三天的高考，一定要和孩子在一起。",py:"Zǎoshang jiǔ diǎn, kǎoshì kāishǐ. Yǒude fùmǔ mǎshàng huíjiā gěi háizi zhǔnbèi wǔfàn, gèng duō de fùmǔ huì liú zài kǎochǎng wàimiàn děng háizi. Suīrán bù shǎo fùmǔ gōngzuò máng, hěn nán qǐngjià, dànshì tāmen dōu juéde gāokǎo hé jiéhūn, shēng háizi yíyàng, shì yìshēng zhǐyǒu yí cì de dàshì, suǒyǐ zhè sān tiān de gāokǎo, yídìng yào hé háizi zài yìqǐ.",en:"At nine in the morning, the exam begins. Some parents go straight home to make lunch for their child, but more of them stay outside the exam site and wait. Many parents are busy and find it hard to get time off, but they all feel that the gaokao, like getting married or having a baby, is a big event that happens only once in a lifetime. So for these three days of exams, they must be with their child."},{zh:"其实，从考试前半年甚至一年起，很多考生的父母就已经在做准备了。他们帮孩子制订复习计划，安排日常生活，并带孩子参加各种辅导班。有的父母每天都陪着孩子复习，孩子睡了自己才睡，甚至每天夜里还要起床看看孩子，怕孩子感冒生病。第二天早上六点多，又要叫孩子起床上学。这样的考试不只是对考生一个人的考验，也是对他们一家人的考验。",py:"Qíshí, cóng kǎoshì qián bàn nián shènzhì yì nián qǐ, hěn duō kǎoshēng de fùmǔ jiù yǐjīng zài zuò zhǔnbèi le. Tāmen bāng háizi zhìdìng fùxí jìhuà, ānpái rìcháng shēnghuó, bìng dài háizi cānjiā gè zhǒng fǔdǎobān. Yǒude fùmǔ měi tiān dōu péizhe háizi fùxí, háizi shuì le zìjǐ cái shuì, shènzhì měi tiān yèli hái yào qǐchuáng kànkan háizi, pà háizi gǎnmào shēngbìng. Dì-èr tiān zǎoshang liù diǎn duō, yòu yào jiào háizi qǐchuáng shàngxué. Zhèyàng de kǎoshì bù zhǐ shì duì kǎoshēng yí gè rén de kǎoyàn, yě shì duì tāmen yì jiā rén de kǎoyàn.",en:"In fact, half a year or even a year before the exam, many parents have already started preparing. They help their child make a study plan, organize daily life, and take the child to all kinds of tutoring classes. Some parents study with their child every day and only go to bed after the child is asleep. Some even get up every night to check on the child, afraid the child will catch a cold or get sick. Then a little after six the next morning, they have to wake the child up for school again. An exam like this is not just a test for the student, but a test for the whole family."}],vocab:[],points:[],think:[],tf:[],mc:[],tip:null},{n:13,title:"8月8日，我们结婚",py:"8 yuè 8 rì, wǒmen jiéhūn",en:"August 8: Our Wedding Day",chars:352,daodu:"",daoduEn:"",paras:[{zh:"8月8日的早上8点，你会发现北京的大路小路上，忽然出现了很多系着鲜花和红气球的汽车。这天中午，你又会发现不少饭店门口都有很多人，他们高兴地等在那里。为什么会这样呢？因为中国人认为这一天是结婚的好日子。",py:"8 yuè 8 rì de zǎoshang 8 diǎn, nǐ huì fāxiàn Běijīng de dàlù xiǎolù shang, hūrán chūxiànle hěn duō jìzhe xiānhuā hé hóng qìqiú de qìchē. Zhè tiān zhōngwǔ, nǐ yòu huì fāxiàn bù shǎo fàndiàn ménkǒu dōu yǒu hěn duō rén, tāmen gāoxìng de děng zài nàlǐ. Wèi shénme huì zhèyàng ne? Yīnwèi Zhōngguórén rènwéi zhè yì tiān shì jiéhūn de hǎo rìzi.",en:"At 8 a.m. on August 8, you'll find that lots of cars decorated with fresh flowers and red balloons suddenly appear on Beijing's streets, big and small. At noon that day, you'll also find crowds of people outside many restaurants, happily waiting there. Why is that? Because Chinese people think this is a good day to get married."},{zh:"除了8月8日，中国人还喜欢在2月2日、6月6日、10月10日等日子结婚，因为这些日子的“月”和“日”都是双数，两个人就会“一双一对”。“5”因为听起来有点儿像“幸福”的“福”，所以也很受欢迎。9月9日这天，结婚的人也特别多，因为在汉语里，“9”和“久”的发音一样，有“永远”的意思。",py:"Chúle 8 yuè 8 rì, Zhōngguórén hái xǐhuan zài 2 yuè 2 rì, 6 yuè 6 rì, 10 yuè 10 rì děng rìzi jiéhūn, yīnwèi zhèxiē rìzi de “yuè” hé “rì” dōu shì shuāngshù, liǎng gè rén jiù huì “yì shuāng yí duì”. “5” yīnwèi tīng qilai yǒudiǎnr xiàng “xìngfú” de “fú”, suǒyǐ yě hěn shòu huānyíng. 9 yuè 9 rì zhè tiān, jiéhūn de rén yě tèbié duō, yīnwèi zài Hànyǔ li, “9” hé “jiǔ” de fāyīn yíyàng, yǒu “yǒngyuǎn” de yìsi.",en:'Besides August 8, Chinese people also like to get married on dates such as February 2, June 6 and October 10, because the month and the day of these dates are both even numbers, so the couple will be "a perfect pair." "5" (wǔ) is popular too, because it sounds a bit like "fú" in "xìngfú" (幸福, happiness). Lots of people also get married on September 9, because in Chinese "9" (jiǔ) sounds the same as 久 (jiǔ, "long-lasting"), which suggests "forever."'},{zh:"讲究结婚的日期是中国人的老习惯。但是有一些传统婚礼的习俗，经过了几千年的时间，由于各种原因，现在已经看不到了。比如，在过去的婚礼上，新娘从头到脚都应该穿红色，从婚礼开始到结束，新娘头上一直盖着一块红布，新娘看不到新郎，新郎和其他人也都看不到新娘的脸。而现在，新娘头上已经不用盖什么东西了，她们一般都穿白色的婚纱，或者先穿白色的婚纱，婚礼中间休息的时候再换成红色的旗袍。",py:"Jiǎngjiu jiéhūn de rìqī shì Zhōngguórén de lǎo xíguàn. Dànshì yǒu yìxiē chuántǒng hūnlǐ de xísú, jīngguòle jǐ qiān nián de shíjiān, yóuyú gè zhǒng yuányīn, xiànzài yǐjīng kànbudào le. Bǐrú, zài guòqù de hūnlǐ shang, xīnniáng cóng tóu dào jiǎo dōu yīnggāi chuān hóngsè, cóng hūnlǐ kāishǐ dào jiéshù, xīnniáng tóu shang yìzhí gàizhe yí kuài hóng bù, xīnniáng kànbudào xīnláng, xīnláng hé qítā rén yě dōu kànbudào xīnniáng de liǎn. Ér xiànzài, xīnniáng tóu shang yǐjīng búyòng gài shénme dōngxi le, tāmen yìbān dōu chuān báisè de hūnshā, huòzhě xiān chuān báisè de hūnshā, hūnlǐ zhōngjiān xiūxi de shíhou zài huànchéng hóngsè de qípáo.",en:"Choosing a wedding date carefully is an old Chinese custom. But some traditional wedding customs, after thousands of years and for various reasons, can no longer be seen today. For example, at weddings in the past, the bride had to wear red from head to toe, and from the start of the wedding to the end, her head was covered with a piece of red cloth. The bride couldn't see the groom, and the groom and everyone else couldn't see her face. Today, brides no longer cover their heads with anything. They usually wear a white wedding dress, or they wear a white wedding dress first and change into a red qipao during a break in the wedding."}],vocab:[],points:[],think:[],tf:[],mc:[],tip:null},{n:14,title:"自相矛盾",py:"Zìxiāng máodùn",en:"One's Own Spear Against One's Own Shield",chars:262,daodu:"",daoduEn:"",paras:[{zh:"矛和盾都是中国古代常用的兵器。矛可以用来刺杀敌人，盾可以用来保护自己。“自相矛盾”是一个很常用的成语，关于这个成语有一个非常有趣的故事。",py:"Máo hé dùn dōu shì Zhōngguó gǔdài chángyòng de bīngqì. Máo kěyǐ yònglái cìshā dírén, dùn kěyǐ yònglái bǎohù zìjǐ. “Zìxiāng máodùn” shì yí gè hěn chángyòng de chéngyǔ, guānyú zhège chéngyǔ yǒu yí gè fēicháng yǒuqù de gùshi.",en:`Spears and shields were both common weapons in ancient China. A spear was used to stab enemies, and a shield was used to protect yourself. "Zìxiāng máodùn" (自相矛盾, "one's own spear against one's own shield") is a very common idiom, and there is a very interesting story behind it.`},{zh:"从前，楚国有个卖兵器的人，在市场上卖矛和盾。他一见到人就说，他的矛和盾都是世界上最好的，可还是没有人买。",py:"Cóngqián, Chǔguó yǒu gè mài bīngqì de rén, zài shìchǎng shang mài máo hé dùn. Tā yí jiàndào rén jiù shuō, tā de máo hé dùn dōu shì shìjiè shang zuì hǎo de, kě háishi méiyǒu rén mǎi.",en:"Long ago, in the State of Chu, there was a man who sold weapons. He sold spears and shields at the market. Whenever he saw people, he told them his spears and shields were the best in the world, but still nobody bought any."},{zh:"最后，他举起盾向周围的人大声说：“快来看我的盾啊，我卖的盾是最坚固的，世界上任何东西都不能刺穿它。”过了一会儿，他又举起矛向人们炫耀：“快来看我的矛吧，它是最锋利的，无论多么坚固的盾都能刺穿！”听到这里，大家都笑了，觉得他在吹牛。有人就问他：“如果用你的矛来刺你的盾，会怎么样呢？”那个人听了，一句话也回答不出来。",py:"Zuìhòu, tā jǔqǐ dùn xiàng zhōuwéi de rén dàshēng shuō: “Kuài lái kàn wǒ de dùn a, wǒ mài de dùn shì zuì jiāngù de, shìjiè shang rènhé dōngxi dōu bù néng cìchuān tā.” Guòle yíhuìr, tā yòu jǔqǐ máo xiàng rénmen xuànyào: “Kuài lái kàn wǒ de máo ba, tā shì zuì fēnglì de, wúlùn duōme jiāngù de dùn dōu néng cìchuān!” Tīngdào zhèlǐ, dàjiā dōu xiào le, juéde tā zài chuīniú. Yǒu rén jiù wèn tā: “Rúguǒ yòng nǐ de máo lái cì nǐ de dùn, huì zěnmeyàng ne?” Nàge rén tīng le, yí jù huà yě huídá bu chūlái.",en:`At last, he held up a shield and shouted to the people around him: "Come and see my shield! The shields I sell are the strongest. Nothing in the world can pierce them." After a while, he held up a spear and boasted: "Come and see my spear! It's the sharpest. It can pierce any shield, no matter how strong!" Hearing this, everyone laughed, thinking he was bragging. Someone asked him: "What would happen if you stabbed your shield with your spear?" The man couldn't say a single word in reply.`},{zh:"后来，人们就用“自相矛盾”来比喻说话、做事前后不一样。",py:"Hòulái, rénmen jiù yòng “zìxiāng máodùn” lái bǐyù shuōhuà, zuòshì qiánhòu bù yíyàng.",en:'Later, people began to use "zìxiāng máodùn" to describe words or actions that contradict themselves.'}],vocab:[],points:[],think:[],tf:[],mc:[],tip:null},{n:15,title:"中国的茶馆",py:"Zhōngguó de cháguǎn",en:"Chinese Teahouses",chars:345,daodu:"",daoduEn:"",paras:[{zh:"你可能去过大饭店，去过咖啡馆，也可能去过歌厅什么的，可是你有没有去过中国的茶馆呢？",py:"Nǐ kěnéng qùguo dà fàndiàn, qùguo kāfēiguǎn, yě kěnéng qùguo gētīng shénme de, kěshì nǐ yǒu méiyǒu qùguo Zhōngguó de cháguǎn ne?",en:"You may have been to big restaurants and cafés, and maybe to karaoke halls and places like that, but have you ever been to a Chinese teahouse?"},{zh:"在中国，几乎每个城市都有茶馆，特别是南方的一些省市，那里的茶馆几乎和饭馆一样多。不仅城市的马路边有茶馆，公园里有茶馆，甚至农村都有茶馆了。很多人都有去茶馆的习惯。有些人一大早就到茶馆喝茶，有些人下班后到那里坐上两三个小时，或读书看报，或一边喝茶，一边聊天。到了节假日，朋友们也常常到茶馆里聚会。有些茶馆还经常有各种文化活动。总之，茶馆不但是人们休息的地方，也是人们交流的重要地方，同时，也为国内外的游客提供了一个了解当地文化的机会。",py:"Zài Zhōngguó, jīhū měi gè chéngshì dōu yǒu cháguǎn, tèbié shì nánfāng de yìxiē shěng shì, nàlǐ de cháguǎn jīhū hé fànguǎn yíyàng duō. Bùjǐn chéngshì de mǎlù biān yǒu cháguǎn, gōngyuán li yǒu cháguǎn, shènzhì nóngcūn dōu yǒu cháguǎn le. Hěn duō rén dōu yǒu qù cháguǎn de xíguàn. Yǒuxiē rén yídàzǎo jiù dào cháguǎn hē chá, yǒuxiē rén xiàbān hòu dào nàlǐ zuòshang liǎng-sān gè xiǎoshí, huò dú shū kàn bào, huò yìbiān hē chá, yìbiān liáotiān. Dàole jiéjiàrì, péngyoumen yě chángcháng dào cháguǎn li jùhuì. Yǒuxiē cháguǎn hái jīngcháng yǒu gè zhǒng wénhuà huódòng. Zǒngzhī, cháguǎn búdàn shì rénmen xiūxi de dìfang, yě shì rénmen jiāoliú de zhòngyào dìfang, tóngshí, yě wèi guónèiwài de yóukè tígōngle yí gè liǎojiě dāngdì wénhuà de jīhuì.",en:"In China, almost every city has teahouses. In some southern provinces and cities especially, there are almost as many teahouses as restaurants. There are teahouses not only along city streets and in parks, but even in the countryside. Many people have the habit of going to teahouses. Some go for tea first thing in the morning; others go after work and sit there for two or three hours, reading books and newspapers, or chatting over tea. On holidays, friends often get together in teahouses too. Some teahouses also often hold all kinds of cultural events. In short, teahouses are not only places to relax but also important places for people to meet and talk. They also give visitors from China and abroad a chance to learn about local culture."},{zh:"北京的茶馆也不少，其中最有名的是前门附近的老舍茶馆。客人一坐进老舍茶馆，服务员小姐马上就会送来一壶热茶和几种北京小吃。客人可以一边吃着、喝着，一边看中国传统的京剧、杂技等节目。现在，老舍茶馆已经成为一处新的旅游景点，每天都吸引着不少中外游客来参观。",py:"Běijīng de cháguǎn yě bù shǎo, qízhōng zuì yǒumíng de shì Qiánmén fùjìn de Lǎoshě Cháguǎn. Kèrén yí zuòjìn Lǎoshě Cháguǎn, fúwùyuán xiǎojiě mǎshàng jiù huì sònglái yì hú rè chá hé jǐ zhǒng Běijīng xiǎochī. Kèrén kěyǐ yìbiān chīzhe, hēzhe, yìbiān kàn Zhōngguó chuántǒng de jīngjù, zájì děng jiémù. Xiànzài, Lǎoshě Cháguǎn yǐjīng chéngwéi yí chù xīn de lǚyóu jǐngdiǎn, měi tiān dōu xīyǐnzhe bù shǎo zhōngwài yóukè lái cānguān.",en:"Beijing has lots of teahouses too, and the most famous is the Lao She Teahouse near Qianmen. As soon as guests sit down in the Lao She Teahouse, a waitress brings them a pot of hot tea and a few kinds of Beijing snacks. Guests can eat and drink while watching traditional Chinese shows such as Peking Opera and acrobatics. Today the Lao She Teahouse has become a new tourist attraction, and it draws many Chinese and foreign visitors every day."}],vocab:[],points:[],think:[],tf:[],mc:[],tip:null},{n:16,title:"海龟和海带",py:"Hǎiguī hé hǎidài",en:'"Sea Turtles" and "Kelp"',chars:257,daodu:"",daoduEn:"",paras:[{zh:"古代中国人认为自己的国家在大海的中间，别的国家都在大海以外很远的地方。所以，他们说自己的国家是“海内”，说别的国家是“海外”。直到现在，人们还是这样说。“去海外”就是“出国；去外国”的意思。",py:"Gǔdài Zhōngguórén rènwéi zìjǐ de guójiā zài dàhǎi de zhōngjiān, bié de guójiā dōu zài dàhǎi yǐwài hěn yuǎn de dìfang. Suǒyǐ, tāmen shuō zìjǐ de guójiā shì “hǎinèi”, shuō bié de guójiā shì “hǎiwài”. Zhídào xiànzài, rénmen háishi zhèyàng shuō. “Qù hǎiwài” jiù shì “chūguó; qù wàiguó” de yìsi.",en:'The ancient Chinese believed their country lay in the middle of the sea, and that other countries were far away beyond the sea. So they called their own country "hǎinèi" (within the seas) and other countries "hǎiwài" (beyond the seas). People still say it this way today. "Qù hǎiwài" means "to go abroad; to go to a foreign country."'},{zh:"中国人很早就开始去海外留学，但是直到1980年以后，去海外留学的人才多了起来。因为他们学习了先进的知识和技术，还会说外语，所以毕业回国后，都有很好的工作和收入。人们把这些从海外留学归来的人称为“海归”（海龟）。",py:"Zhōngguórén hěn zǎo jiù kāishǐ qù hǎiwài liúxué, dànshì zhídào 1980 nián yǐhòu, qù hǎiwài liúxué de rén cái duōle qilai. Yīnwèi tāmen xuéxíle xiānjìn de zhīshi hé jìshù, hái huì shuō wàiyǔ, suǒyǐ bìyè huíguó hòu, dōu yǒu hěn hǎo de gōngzuò hé shōurù. Rénmen bǎ zhèxiē cóng hǎiwài liúxué guīlái de rén chēngwéi “hǎiguī” (hǎiguī).",en:'Chinese people began going abroad to study long ago, but it was only after 1980 that the number of overseas students really grew. Because they had learned advanced knowledge and technology and could speak foreign languages, they all found good jobs with good pay after graduating and coming home. People call those who come back from studying abroad "hǎiguī" (海归, "returned from overseas"), which sounds just like 海龟, "sea turtle."'},{zh:"后来，“海归”越来越多，找工作也越来越难了。很多“海归”找不到工作，只好等待。于是，人们又把这些从海外留学归来、等待工作机会的人称为“海待”（海带）。",py:"Hòulái, “hǎiguī” yuèláiyuè duō, zhǎo gōngzuò yě yuèláiyuè nán le. Hěn duō “hǎiguī” zhǎobudào gōngzuò, zhǐhǎo děngdài. Yúshì, rénmen yòu bǎ zhèxiē cóng hǎiwài liúxué guīlái, děngdài gōngzuò jīhuì de rén chēngwéi “hǎidài” (hǎidài).",en:`Later, there were more and more "hǎiguī," and finding a job got harder and harder. Many of them couldn't find work and had to wait. So people began calling those who had come back from studying abroad and were waiting for a job "hǎidài" (海待, "waiting after returning from overseas"), which sounds just like 海带, "kelp."`},{zh:"“海归”和“海待”，最早都是在网上使用的词语，因为有趣，所以很快就流行起来了。",py:"“Hǎiguī” hé “hǎidài”, zuì zǎo dōu shì zài wǎngshang shǐyòng de cíyǔ, yīnwèi yǒuqù, suǒyǐ hěn kuài jiù liúxíng qilai le.",en:'"Hǎiguī" and "hǎidài" were both first used online. Because they were fun, they quickly caught on.'}],vocab:[],points:[],think:[],tf:[],mc:[],tip:null},{n:17,title:"神奇的老鼠",py:"Shénqí de lǎoshǔ",en:"The Amazing Mouse",chars:286,daodu:"",daoduEn:"",paras:[{zh:"在非洲有一个马戏团。马戏团人不多，只有六七个人。他们的节目也不多，但很有名，因为他们有一只小老鼠。这种小老鼠只生活在非洲，它能完成这个马戏团最精彩的节目。它表演的节目会吸引很多观众，因为只要不伤害它的头，无论谁都踩不死它。你说神奇不神奇？",py:"Zài Fēizhōu yǒu yí gè mǎxìtuán. Mǎxìtuán rén bù duō, zhǐyǒu liù-qī gè rén. Tāmen de jiémù yě bù duō, dàn hěn yǒumíng, yīnwèi tāmen yǒu yì zhī xiǎo lǎoshǔ. Zhè zhǒng xiǎo lǎoshǔ zhǐ shēnghuó zài Fēizhōu, tā néng wánchéng zhège mǎxìtuán zuì jīngcǎi de jiémù. Tā biǎoyǎn de jiémù huì xīyǐn hěn duō guānzhòng, yīnwèi zhǐyào bù shānghài tā de tóu, wúlùn shéi dōu cǎibusǐ tā. Nǐ shuō shénqí bu shénqí?",en:"There was a circus in Africa. It was small, with only six or seven people. They didn't have many acts, but they were famous because they had a little mouse. This kind of mouse lives only in Africa, and it performed the circus's most exciting act. Its act drew big crowds, because as long as its head isn't hurt, nobody can kill it by stepping on it. Isn't that amazing?"},{zh:"表演开始了。一个人把老鼠放在地上。接着，那个人踩在了它的身上，老鼠立刻被压扁了。然后，那个人站到了旁边。这时，所有的人都看着这只老鼠。神奇的是，被压扁的老鼠竟然没有死！过了一会儿，它像气球一样，一点点地变大了。很快，它变回了原来的样子，还跳了几下。",py:"Biǎoyǎn kāishǐ le. Yí gè rén bǎ lǎoshǔ fàng zài dìshang. Jiēzhe, nàge rén cǎi zàile tā de shēnshang, lǎoshǔ lìkè bèi yābiǎn le. Ránhòu, nàge rén zhàndàole pángbiān. Zhè shí, suǒyǒu de rén dōu kànzhe zhè zhī lǎoshǔ. Shénqí de shì, bèi yābiǎn de lǎoshǔ jìngrán méiyǒu sǐ! Guòle yíhuìr, tā xiàng qìqiú yíyàng, yìdiǎndiǎn de biàndà le. Hěn kuài, tā biànhuíle yuánlái de yàngzi, hái tiàole jǐ xià.",en:"The show began. A man put the mouse on the ground. Then he stepped on it, and the mouse was instantly squashed flat. Then the man stepped aside. Everyone was watching the mouse. Amazingly, the flattened mouse wasn't dead! After a while, it grew bigger little by little, like a balloon. Soon it was back to its normal shape, and it even jumped a few times."},{zh:"这种神奇的老鼠叫做扁鼠。它长得和别的老鼠差不多，但是它的骨头特别坚韧。被东西压住时，它的骨头和肉可以躲开压住它的东西。所以，即使300千克的东西压在它身上也没问题！",py:"Zhè zhǒng shénqí de lǎoshǔ jiàozuò biǎnshǔ. Tā zhǎng de hé bié de lǎoshǔ chàbuduō, dànshì tā de gǔtou tèbié jiānrèn. Bèi dōngxi yāzhù shí, tā de gǔtou hé ròu kěyǐ duǒkāi yāzhù tā de dōngxi. Suǒyǐ, jíshǐ 300 qiānkè de dōngxi yā zài tā shēnshang yě méi wèntí!",en:`This amazing mouse is called the "flat mouse." It looks much like other mice, but its bones are especially tough and flexible. When something presses down on it, its bones and flesh can move out of the way. So even with 300 kilograms on top of it, it's fine!`}],vocab:[],points:[],think:[],tf:[],mc:[],tip:null},{n:18,title:"望京——北京的新韩国城",py:"Wàngjīng — Běijīng de xīn Hánguóchéng",en:"Wangjing: Beijing's New Koreatown",chars:347,daodu:"",daoduEn:"",paras:[{zh:"以前，北京的出租车司机一听客人说韩语，马上就会问：“您是去五道口吧？”现在，这个问题已经变成了：“您是去望京吧？”",py:"Yǐqián, Běijīng de chūzūchē sījī yì tīng kèrén shuō Hányǔ, mǎshàng jiù huì wèn: “Nín shì qù Wǔdàokǒu ba?” Xiànzài, zhège wèntí yǐjīng biànchéngle: “Nín shì qù Wàngjīng ba?”",en:`In the past, as soon as a Beijing taxi driver heard a passenger speak Korean, he would ask right away: "You're going to Wudaokou, right?" Now the question has become: "You're going to Wangjing, right?"`},{zh:"在望京的西园，韩国家庭比中国家庭还多。这里的服务员几乎都会汉韩两种语言。2005年，望京又请来了会韩语的警察、医生和护士。",py:"Zài Wàngjīng de Xīyuán, Hánguó jiātíng bǐ Zhōngguó jiātíng hái duō. Zhèlǐ de fúwùyuán jīhū dōu huì Hàn Hán liǎng zhǒng yǔyán. 2005 nián, Wàngjīng yòu qǐngláile huì Hányǔ de jǐngchá, yīshēng hé hùshi.",en:"In Xiyuan in Wangjing, there are even more Korean families than Chinese ones. Almost all the service staff here speak both Chinese and Korean. In 2005, Wangjing also brought in police officers, doctors and nurses who speak Korean."},{zh:"中国和韩国虽然是邻居，但是两国人的生活习惯还是有许多不同。比如，韩国人习惯把鞋子放到门外，但是中国邻居觉得门前的地方是大家的，一些中国老人甚至还会生气。韩国人订了外卖，吃完以后就会把碗放在家门口，等着饭馆的服务员拿走。中国邻居看了，会觉得很不卫生。同样，韩国人也不明白为什么早上晚上，都有那么多中国人扭秧歌；为什么中国人会把狗带进电梯……",py:"Zhōngguó hé Hánguó suīrán shì línjū, dànshì liǎng guó rén de shēnghuó xíguàn háishi yǒu xǔduō bùtóng. Bǐrú, Hánguórén xíguàn bǎ xiézi fàngdào mén wài, dànshì Zhōngguó línjū juéde mén qián de dìfang shì dàjiā de, yìxiē Zhōngguó lǎorén shènzhì hái huì shēngqì. Hánguórén dìngle wàimài, chīwán yǐhòu jiù huì bǎ wǎn fàng zài jiā ménkǒu, děngzhe fànguǎn de fúwùyuán názǒu. Zhōngguó línjū kàn le, huì juéde hěn bú wèishēng. Tóngyàng, Hánguórén yě bù míngbai wèi shénme zǎoshang wǎnshang, dōu yǒu nàme duō Zhōngguórén niǔ yāngge; wèi shénme Zhōngguórén huì bǎ gǒu dàijìn diàntī...",en:"China and Korea are neighbors, but people from the two countries still have many different habits. For example, Koreans usually leave their shoes outside the door, but their Chinese neighbors feel the space in front of the door belongs to everyone, and some older Chinese people even get angry. When Koreans order takeout, they put the bowls outside their door after eating for the restaurant staff to collect. Their Chinese neighbors find this very unhygienic. In the same way, Koreans don't understand why so many Chinese people do the yangge dance every morning and evening, or why Chinese people take their dogs into the elevator..."},{zh:"经过十几年的时间，在这里，中韩家庭的不同习惯已经不再是问题，年轻的韩国人就更加适应这里的生活了。他们从小就生活在这里，还在北京上了大学。他们的汉语说得不但流利而且非常地道。他们的朋友里面，中国人甚至比韩国人还多。",py:"Jīngguò shíjǐ nián de shíjiān, zài zhèlǐ, Zhōng Hán jiātíng de bùtóng xíguàn yǐjīng bú zài shì wèntí, niánqīng de Hánguórén jiù gèngjiā shìyìng zhèlǐ de shēnghuó le. Tāmen cóngxiǎo jiù shēnghuó zài zhèlǐ, hái zài Běijīng shàngle dàxué. Tāmen de Hànyǔ shuō de búdàn liúlì érqiě fēicháng dìdao. Tāmen de péngyou lǐmiàn, Zhōngguórén shènzhì bǐ Hánguórén hái duō.",en:"After more than ten years, the different habits of Chinese and Korean families here are no longer a problem, and young Koreans feel even more at home here. They grew up here and went to university in Beijing. Their Chinese is not only fluent but also very natural. Among their friends, there are even more Chinese than Koreans."}],vocab:[],points:[],think:[],tf:[],mc:[],tip:null},{n:19,title:"“万”字难写",py:"“Wàn” zì nán xiě",en:"The Character 万 Is Hard to Write",chars:380,daodu:"",daoduEn:"",paras:[{zh:"从前，有一位老人，他家里的人都是文盲，连最简单的字都不认识。于是，他就请了一位老师教他儿子认字。第一天上学，老师用毛笔在白纸上写了一笔，告诉他儿子说：“这是‘一’字。”他儿子学得很认真，记住了，回去后就写给父亲看：“我学了一个字——‘一’。”老人非常满意。",py:"Cóngqián, yǒu yí wèi lǎorén, tā jiā li de rén dōu shì wénmáng, lián zuì jiǎndān de zì dōu bú rènshi. Yúshì, tā jiù qǐngle yí wèi lǎoshī jiāo tā érzi rèn zì. Dì-yī tiān shàngxué, lǎoshī yòng máobǐ zài bái zhǐ shang xiěle yì bǐ, gàosu tā érzi shuō: “Zhè shì ‘yī’ zì.” Tā érzi xué de hěn rènzhēn, jìzhù le, huíqù hòu jiù xiě gěi fùqin kàn: “Wǒ xuéle yí gè zì — ‘yī’.” Lǎorén fēicháng mǎnyì.",en:`Long ago there was an old man whose whole family was illiterate. They couldn't read even the simplest characters. So he hired a teacher to teach his son to read. On the first day of school, the teacher wrote one stroke on white paper with a brush and told the son: "This is the character 一 (yī, one)." The son studied hard and remembered it. When he got home, he wrote it for his father: "I learned a character: 一 (one)." The old man was very pleased.`},{zh:"第二天，老师又用毛笔在纸上写了两笔，说：“这是‘二’字。”这次，儿子不觉得有什么新鲜了。到了第三天，老师用毛笔在纸上写了三笔，说：“这是个‘三’字。”儿子学完就高兴地跑回家，对父亲说：“学习认字太容易了，不用花这么多钱请老师了！”看到儿子这么聪明，老人很快就辞退了老师。",py:"Dì-èr tiān, lǎoshī yòu yòng máobǐ zài zhǐ shang xiěle liǎng bǐ, shuō: “Zhè shì ‘èr’ zì.” Zhè cì, érzi bù juéde yǒu shénme xīnxiān le. Dàole dì-sān tiān, lǎoshī yòng máobǐ zài zhǐ shang xiěle sān bǐ, shuō: “Zhè shì gè ‘sān’ zì.” Érzi xuéwán jiù gāoxìng de pǎohuí jiā, duì fùqin shuō: “Xuéxí rèn zì tài róngyì le, búyòng huā zhème duō qián qǐng lǎoshī le!” Kàndào érzi zhème cōngming, lǎorén hěn kuài jiù cítuìle lǎoshī.",en:`The next day, the teacher wrote two strokes on the paper and said: "This is 二 (èr, two)." This time, the son didn't find it anything new. On the third day, the teacher wrote three strokes and said: "This is 三 (sān, three)." After the lesson, the son ran home happily and said to his father: "Learning characters is too easy! We don't need to spend so much money on a teacher!" Seeing how clever his son was, the old man soon sent the teacher away.`},{zh:"过了几天，老人想请一位姓万的朋友来喝酒，就让儿子早上起来写个请柬。时间慢慢地过去，天快黑了，儿子还没写好。老人有点儿着急了，就跑到儿子房间里看。",py:"Guòle jǐ tiān, lǎorén xiǎng qǐng yí wèi xìng Wàn de péngyou lái hē jiǔ, jiù ràng érzi zǎoshang qǐlai xiě gè qǐngjiǎn. Shíjiān mànmàn de guòqù, tiān kuài hēi le, érzi hái méi xiěhǎo. Lǎorén yǒudiǎnr zháojí le, jiù pǎodào érzi fángjiān li kàn.",en:"A few days later, the old man wanted to invite a friend surnamed Wan over for a drink, so he told his son to get up in the morning and write an invitation. Time slowly passed, and it was almost dark, but the son still hadn't finished. The old man got a little worried and ran to his son's room to take a look."},{zh:"进门后，他见儿子正苦着脸坐在桌边，手里拿着一把梳子在一张长长的纸上画着。一见父亲进来，儿子就抱怨说：“有那么多的姓，他为什么姓‘万’呢？我拿来了母亲的梳子，一次可以写二十多笔。可是从一大早写到现在，手都疼了，也只写了三千多笔！‘万’字真难写呀！”",py:"Jìn mén hòu, tā jiàn érzi zhèng kǔzhe liǎn zuò zài zhuō biān, shǒu li názhe yì bǎ shūzi zài yì zhāng chángcháng de zhǐ shang huàzhe. Yí jiàn fùqin jìnlai, érzi jiù bàoyuàn shuō: “Yǒu nàme duō de xìng, tā wèi shénme xìng ‘Wàn’ ne? Wǒ náláile mǔqin de shūzi, yí cì kěyǐ xiě èrshí duō bǐ. Kěshì cóng yídàzǎo xiědào xiànzài, shǒu dōu téng le, yě zhǐ xiěle sānqiān duō bǐ! ‘Wàn’ zì zhēn nán xiě ya!”",en:`When he walked in, he saw his son sitting at the desk with a pained face, holding a comb and drawing on a long, long sheet of paper. As soon as he saw his father come in, the son complained: "There are so many surnames. Why does he have to be called 'Wan'? I got Mother's comb, so I can write more than twenty strokes at a time. But I've been writing since early this morning, my hand hurts, and I've only done three thousand strokes! 'Wan' is so hard to write!" (万 wàn means "ten thousand," so the son thought it needed ten thousand strokes.)`}],vocab:[],points:[],think:[],tf:[],mc:[],tip:null},{n:20,title:"不要忘了寄信",py:"Búyào wàngle jì xìn",en:"Don't Forget to Mail the Letter",chars:327,daodu:"",daoduEn:"",paras:[{zh:"王先生上班前，妻子帮他穿上大衣，把一封信放进他的包里，提醒他说：“在你进办公室之前，千万别忘了寄信。这样姨妈明天早上就可以收到了。这封信非常重要。”",py:"Wáng xiānsheng shàngbān qián, qīzi bāng tā chuānshang dàyī, bǎ yì fēng xìn fàngjìn tā de bāo li, tíxǐng tā shuō: “Zài nǐ jìn bàngōngshì zhīqián, qiānwàn bié wàngle jì xìn. Zhèyàng yímā míngtiān zǎoshang jiù kěyǐ shōudào le. Zhè fēng xìn fēicháng zhòngyào.”",en:`Before Mr. Wang left for work, his wife helped him put on his coat, put a letter into his bag and reminded him: "Before you go into your office, don't forget to mail the letter, whatever you do. That way Auntie will get it tomorrow morning. This letter is very important."`},{zh:"可是路上王先生偏偏忘了寄信的事。他在城里下了火车，急急忙忙去上班，信还躺在他的包里呢。快离开火车站的时候，一位陌生的先生走过来，拍拍他说：“别忘了你的信！”王先生这才想起了妻子的话，马上向附近的邮箱跑去。这时，又一位陌生人对他说：“先生，不要忘了寄信！”",py:"Kěshì lùshang Wáng xiānsheng piānpiān wàngle jì xìn de shì. Tā zài chéng li xiàle huǒchē, jíjímángmáng qù shàngbān, xìn hái tǎng zài tā de bāo li ne. Kuài líkāi huǒchēzhàn de shíhou, yí wèi mòshēng de xiānsheng zǒu guòlai, pāipai tā shuō: “Bié wàngle nǐ de xìn!” Wáng xiānsheng zhè cái xiǎngqǐle qīzi de huà, mǎshàng xiàng fùjìn de yóuxiāng pǎoqù. Zhè shí, yòu yí wèi mòshēngrén duì tā shuō: “Xiānsheng, búyào wàngle jì xìn!”",en:`But on the way, Mr. Wang forgot all about the letter. He got off the train in the city and hurried off to work, with the letter still lying in his bag. Just as he was leaving the train station, a gentleman he didn't know came up, patted him and said: "Don't forget your letter!" Only then did Mr. Wang remember his wife's words, and he ran straight to a nearby mailbox. Just then, another stranger said to him: "Sir, don't forget to mail your letter!"`},{zh:"王先生感到很奇怪，他把信投入邮箱，立刻离开了火车站。没走多远，一位和蔼可亲的女士微笑着问他：“先生，你没忘了寄信吧？”王先生非常惊讶，怎么世界上所有的人都来提醒他寄信呢？他忍不住问这位女士：“你们怎么都知道我得寄一封信呢？我早就把信放到邮箱里了。”那位女士大笑之后告诉他说：“你的妻子在你的大衣上贴了一张纸条，上面写着：请告诉我的丈夫，他应该寄一封信！”",py:"Wáng xiānsheng gǎndào hěn qíguài, tā bǎ xìn tóurù yóuxiāng, lìkè líkāile huǒchēzhàn. Méi zǒu duō yuǎn, yí wèi hé'ǎi kěqīn de nǚshì wēixiàozhe wèn tā: “Xiānsheng, nǐ méi wàngle jì xìn ba?” Wáng xiānsheng fēicháng jīngyà, zěnme shìjiè shang suǒyǒu de rén dōu lái tíxǐng tā jì xìn ne? Tā rěnbuzhù wèn zhè wèi nǚshì: “Nǐmen zěnme dōu zhīdào wǒ děi jì yì fēng xìn ne? Wǒ zǎo jiù bǎ xìn fàngdào yóuxiāng li le.” Nà wèi nǚshì dà xiào zhīhòu gàosu tā shuō: “Nǐ de qīzi zài nǐ de dàyī shang tiēle yì zhāng zhǐtiáo, shàngmiàn xiězhe: qǐng gàosu wǒ de zhàngfu, tā yīnggāi jì yì fēng xìn!”",en:`Mr. Wang found this very strange. He dropped the letter into the mailbox and left the station right away. Before he had gone far, a kind, friendly lady smiled and asked him: "Sir, you didn't forget to mail your letter, did you?" Mr. Wang was astonished. Why was everyone in the world reminding him to mail a letter? He couldn't help asking the lady: "How do you all know I have to mail a letter? I put it in the mailbox long ago." The lady burst out laughing and told him: "Your wife stuck a note on your coat. It says: Please tell my husband he should mail a letter!"`}],vocab:[],points:[],think:[],tf:[],mc:[],tip:null},{n:21,title:"梨和苹果的故事",py:"Lí hé píngguǒ de gùshi",en:"Stories of a Pear and an Apple",chars:364,daodu:"",daoduEn:"",paras:[{zh:"今天给大家讲两个故事。一个是“孔融（Kong Rong）让梨”。孔融是中国汉代的文学家。他小时候很聪明，而且很有礼貌，父母都非常喜欢他。一天，父亲买了一些梨，而且拿了一个最大的给孔融。孔融却摇摇头，拿了一个最小的梨说：“我年纪最小，应该吃小的梨。那个大梨就给哥哥吧。”父亲听后非常高兴。",py:"Jīntiān gěi dàjiā jiǎng liǎng gè gùshi. Yí gè shì “Kǒng Róng (Kong Rong) ràng lí”. Kǒng Róng shì Zhōngguó Hàndài de wénxuéjiā. Tā xiǎoshíhou hěn cōngming, érqiě hěn yǒu lǐmào, fùmǔ dōu fēicháng xǐhuan tā. Yì tiān, fùqin mǎile yìxiē lí, érqiě nále yí gè zuì dà de gěi Kǒng Róng. Kǒng Róng què yáoyao tóu, nále yí gè zuì xiǎo de lí shuō: “Wǒ niánjì zuì xiǎo, yīnggāi chī xiǎo de lí. Nàge dà lí jiù gěi gēge ba.” Fùqin tīng hòu fēicháng gāoxìng.",en:`Today I'll tell you two stories. The first is "Kong Rong Gives Up the Bigger Pear." Kong Rong was a writer of China's Han dynasty. As a child he was very clever and very polite, and his parents loved him dearly. One day his father bought some pears and gave the biggest one to Kong Rong. But Kong Rong shook his head, took the smallest pear and said: "I'm the youngest, so I should eat a small pear. Give the big one to my older brother." His father was very happy to hear this.`},{zh:"“孔融让梨”的故事，一直流传到现在，成了许多中国父母教育子女的好例子。它让我们明白了一个美德：把好的东西留给别人，不要总想着自己。",py:"“Kǒng Róng ràng lí” de gùshi, yìzhí liúchuán dào xiànzài, chéngle xǔduō Zhōngguó fùmǔ jiàoyù zǐnǚ de hǎo lìzi. Tā ràng wǒmen míngbaile yí gè měidé: bǎ hǎo de dōngxi liú gěi biérén, búyào zǒng xiǎngzhe zìjǐ.",en:"The story of Kong Rong and the pear has been passed down to this day, and many Chinese parents use it as a good example to teach their children. It teaches us a virtue: leave the good things for others, and don't always think of yourself."},{zh:"另一个故事是“艾森豪威尔（Dwight David Eisenhower）争苹果”，说的是美国前总统艾森豪威尔小时候的故事。有一次，他的妈妈拿来一些苹果，告诉他和他的兄弟们，修草坪修得最好的人可以得到最大最红的苹果。为了得到那个苹果，小艾森豪威尔干得最认真。最后，妈妈把那个最大最红的苹果给了他。艾森豪威尔后来写道：“这件事几乎影响了我一生。它让我明白了，你只有比别人干得更好，才能得到更多！”",py:"Lìng yí gè gùshi shì “Àisēnháowēi'ěr (Dwight David Eisenhower) zhēng píngguǒ”, shuō de shì Měiguó qián zǒngtǒng Àisēnháowēi'ěr xiǎoshíhou de gùshi. Yǒu yí cì, tā de māma nálái yìxiē píngguǒ, gàosu tā hé tā de xiōngdìmen, xiū cǎopíng xiū de zuì hǎo de rén kěyǐ dédào zuì dà zuì hóng de píngguǒ. Wèile dédào nàge píngguǒ, xiǎo Àisēnháowēi'ěr gàn de zuì rènzhēn. Zuìhòu, māma bǎ nàge zuì dà zuì hóng de píngguǒ gěile tā. Àisēnháowēi'ěr hòulái xiědào: “Zhè jiàn shì jīhū yǐngxiǎngle wǒ yìshēng. Tā ràng wǒ míngbaile, nǐ zhǐyǒu bǐ biérén gàn de gèng hǎo, cái néng dédào gèng duō!”",en:`The other story is "Eisenhower Competes for the Apple." It's a story from the childhood of former U.S. President Dwight David Eisenhower. Once his mother brought some apples and told him and his brothers that whoever mowed the lawn best would get the biggest, reddest apple. To win that apple, young Eisenhower worked harder than anyone. In the end, his mother gave him the biggest, reddest apple. Eisenhower later wrote: "This shaped almost my whole life. It taught me that only by doing better than others can you get more!"`},{zh:"孔融和艾森豪威尔后来都成了历史上有名的人物，但这一让一争，却表现了两种不同的思想和文化。",py:"Kǒng Róng hé Àisēnháowēi'ěr hòulái dōu chéngle lìshǐ shang yǒumíng de rénwù, dàn zhè yí ràng yì zhēng, què biǎoxiànle liǎng zhǒng bùtóng de sīxiǎng hé wénhuà.",en:"Kong Rong and Eisenhower both went on to become famous figures in history, but one giving way and the other competing show two different ways of thinking and two different cultures."}],vocab:[],points:[],think:[],tf:[],mc:[],tip:null},{n:22,title:"我在南京的网络生活",py:"Wǒ zài Nánjīng de wǎngluò shēnghuó",en:"My Online Life in Nanjing",chars:312,daodu:"",daoduEn:"",paras:[{zh:"随着网络的发展，现在人们的生活越来越离不开它了。在我的留学生活中，网络也非常重要。比如，我想去南京的任何地方，只要打开“南京公交网”，点一下鼠标，一张电子地图就会立刻出现在我眼前，非常方便。你相信吗，我到南京才半年，可已经差不多走遍南京城了。",py:"Suízhe wǎngluò de fāzhǎn, xiànzài rénmen de shēnghuó yuèláiyuè líbukāi tā le. Zài wǒ de liúxué shēnghuó zhōng, wǎngluò yě fēicháng zhòngyào. Bǐrú, wǒ xiǎng qù Nánjīng de rènhé dìfang, zhǐyào dǎkāi “Nánjīng Gōngjiāo Wǎng”, diǎn yíxià shǔbiāo, yì zhāng diànzǐ dìtú jiù huì lìkè chūxiàn zài wǒ yǎnqián, fēicháng fāngbiàn. Nǐ xiāngxìn ma, wǒ dào Nánjīng cái bàn nián, kě yǐjīng chàbuduō zǒubiàn Nánjīng chéng le.",en:`As the internet develops, people's lives depend on it more and more. In my life as an international student, the internet is very important too. For example, whenever I want to go somewhere in Nanjing, I just open the "Nanjing Public Transit" website and click the mouse, and an electronic map instantly appears in front of me. It's very convenient. Believe it or not, I've only been in Nanjing for half a year, but I've already been almost all over the city.`},{zh:"如果我在饭馆吃到一道好吃的中国菜，我一定记住它的名字。回去后，我会在网上找到它的做法，慢慢学习，这样我就可以在房间里享受自己做的美味了。",py:"Rúguǒ wǒ zài fànguǎn chīdào yí dào hǎochī de Zhōngguó cài, wǒ yídìng jìzhù tā de míngzi. Huíqù hòu, wǒ huì zài wǎngshang zhǎodào tā de zuòfǎ, mànmàn xuéxí, zhèyàng wǒ jiù kěyǐ zài fángjiān li xiǎngshòu zìjǐ zuò de měiwèi le.",en:"If I eat a delicious Chinese dish at a restaurant, I always remember its name. When I get back, I find the recipe online and slowly learn to make it. That way I can enjoy tasty food I made myself, right in my own room."},{zh:"我喜欢听音乐，网上的音乐资源非常丰富，很容易找到好听的歌。我经常找喜欢的中国歌曲，边学边唱“对面的女孩看过来……”、“好一朵美丽的茉莉花……”等等。由于经常练习，我进步很快，还参加了“外国人唱中国歌”的比赛呢！",py:"Wǒ xǐhuan tīng yīnyuè, wǎngshang de yīnyuè zīyuán fēicháng fēngfù, hěn róngyì zhǎodào hǎotīng de gē. Wǒ jīngcháng zhǎo xǐhuan de Zhōngguó gēqǔ, biān xué biān chàng “Duìmiàn de nǚhái kàn guòlai...”, “Hǎo yì duǒ měilì de mòlìhuā...” děngděng. Yóuyú jīngcháng liànxí, wǒ jìnbù hěn kuài, hái cānjiāle “Wàiguórén Chàng Zhōngguó Gē” de bǐsài ne!",en:`I like listening to music. There's a huge amount of music online, so it's easy to find good songs. I often look up Chinese songs I like and learn them as I sing along, such as "Girl across the way, look over here..." and "What a beautiful jasmine flower..." Because I practice a lot, I've improved quickly, and I even took part in a "Foreigners Sing Chinese Songs" contest!`},{zh:"网上购物也很方便。我经常上“易趣网”买衣服和生活用品，上“当当网”和“卓越网”买书。这些网站都送货上门，我只要坐在电脑前点鼠标，一切就都OK了！",py:"Wǎngshang gòuwù yě hěn fāngbiàn. Wǒ jīngcháng shàng “Yìqù Wǎng” mǎi yīfu hé shēnghuó yòngpǐn, shàng “Dāngdāng Wǎng” hé “Zhuóyuè Wǎng” mǎi shū. Zhèxiē wǎngzhàn dōu sòng huò shàngmén, wǒ zhǐyào zuò zài diànnǎo qián diǎn shǔbiāo, yíqiè jiù dōu OK le!",en:"Online shopping is very convenient too. I often go on Eachnet (eBay China) to buy clothes and everyday things, and on Dangdang and Joyo to buy books. These websites all deliver to your door. I just sit at my computer and click the mouse, and everything is OK!"}],vocab:[],points:[],think:[],tf:[],mc:[],tip:null},{n:23,title:"胡同里走出来的明星",py:"Hútòng li zǒu chulai de míngxīng",en:"The Star Who Came Out of a Hutong",chars:363,daodu:"",daoduEn:"",paras:[{zh:"章子怡8岁开始学习跳舞，17岁考进中央戏剧学院，19岁出演张艺谋的电影《我的父亲母亲》，21岁又因为《卧虎藏龙》的成功走向了世界，25岁已经成为国际明星。10年前，没有人能想到，这个从胡同里走出来的女孩儿能这样成功。",py:"Zhāng Zǐyí 8 suì kāishǐ xuéxí tiàowǔ, 17 suì kǎojìn Zhōngyāng Xìjù Xuéyuàn, 19 suì chūyǎn Zhāng Yìmóu de diànyǐng “Wǒ de Fùqin Mǔqin”, 21 suì yòu yīnwèi “Wòhǔ Cánglóng” de chénggōng zǒuxiàngle shìjiè, 25 suì yǐjīng chéngwéi guójì míngxīng. 10 nián qián, méiyǒu rén néng xiǎngdào, zhège cóng hútòng li zǒu chulai de nǚháir néng zhèyàng chénggōng.",en:`Zhang Ziyi began learning dance at 8. At 17 she got into the Central Academy of Drama; at 19 she starred in Zhang Yimou's film "The Road Home"; at 21 she became known around the world thanks to the success of "Crouching Tiger, Hidden Dragon"; and by 25 she was already an international star. Ten years earlier, no one could have imagined that this girl from a hutong would be so successful.`},{zh:"生长在北京的章子怡小时候是一个普通的孩子。她的母亲是幼儿园老师，所以她小时候最大的心愿，就是长大后能当幼儿园老师。因为身体不太好，父母就送她去学跳舞，希望她的身体能变得强壮一些。章子怡说：“虽然每个周末都去学跳舞，但是我更希望周末能去公园。可是爸爸妈妈工作都非常辛苦，还要照顾我和哥哥，到了星期天，已经累得不可能带我们出去玩儿了。”那时，章子怡还常常希望能看到家门口多几辆自行车。每次看到有别人的自行车停在自己家门前，她都特别高兴，因为如果家里来了客人，就会很热闹。",py:"Shēngzhǎng zài Běijīng de Zhāng Zǐyí xiǎoshíhou shì yí gè pǔtōng de háizi. Tā de mǔqin shì yòu'éryuán lǎoshī, suǒyǐ tā xiǎoshíhou zuì dà de xīnyuàn, jiù shì zhǎngdà hòu néng dāng yòu'éryuán lǎoshī. Yīnwèi shēntǐ bú tài hǎo, fùmǔ jiù sòng tā qù xué tiàowǔ, xīwàng tā de shēntǐ néng biàn de qiángzhuàng yìxiē. Zhāng Zǐyí shuō: “Suīrán měi gè zhōumò dōu qù xué tiàowǔ, dànshì wǒ gèng xīwàng zhōumò néng qù gōngyuán. Kěshì bàba māma gōngzuò dōu fēicháng xīnkǔ, hái yào zhàogù wǒ hé gēge, dàole xīngqītiān, yǐjīng lèi de bù kěnéng dài wǒmen chūqù wánr le.” Nà shí, Zhāng Zǐyí hái chángcháng xīwàng néng kàndào jiā ménkǒu duō jǐ liàng zìxíngchē. Měi cì kàndào yǒu biérén de zìxíngchē tíng zài zìjǐ jiā mén qián, tā dōu tèbié gāoxìng, yīnwèi rúguǒ jiā li láile kèrén, jiù huì hěn rènao.",en:`Zhang Ziyi grew up in Beijing as an ordinary child. Her mother was a kindergarten teacher, so her biggest wish as a little girl was to become a kindergarten teacher when she grew up. Because she wasn't very healthy, her parents sent her to learn dance, hoping it would make her a bit stronger. Zhang Ziyi said: "I went to dance class every weekend, but I really wanted to go to the park instead. But Mom and Dad both worked very hard and also had to look after my brother and me. By Sunday they were far too tired to take us out to play." Back then, Zhang Ziyi often hoped to see a few more bicycles outside her door. Every time she saw someone else's bicycle parked in front of her home, she was especially happy, because guests at home meant a lively house.`},{zh:"11岁时，章子怡考上了中国最好的舞蹈学校。那里对学生身材的要求非常高，在当年的两千多个孩子里，章子怡是唯一一个被录取的。这也是她以后走上“明星路”的开始。",py:"11 suì shí, Zhāng Zǐyí kǎoshangle Zhōngguó zuì hǎo de wǔdǎo xuéxiào. Nàlǐ duì xuéshēng shēncái de yāoqiú fēicháng gāo, zài dāngnián de liǎngqiān duō gè háizi li, Zhāng Zǐyí shì wéiyī yí gè bèi lùqǔ de. Zhè yě shì tā yǐhòu zǒushang “míngxīng lù” de kāishǐ.",en:"At 11, Zhang Ziyi passed the entrance exam for the best dance school in China. The school was very strict about students' body shape: of the more than two thousand children who tried that year, Zhang Ziyi was the only one accepted. This was also the start of her road to stardom."}],vocab:[],points:[],think:[],tf:[],mc:[],tip:null},{n:24,title:"唐诗两首",py:"Tángshī liǎng shǒu",en:"Two Tang Poems",chars:213,daodu:"",daoduEn:"",paras:[{zh:"春晓",py:"Chūn Xiǎo",en:"Spring Dawn",fmt:"h"},{zh:"孟浩然",py:"Mèng Hàorán",en:"Meng Haoran",fmt:"poem"},{zh:"春眠不觉晓，",py:"Chūn mián bù jué xiǎo,",en:"Sleeping in spring, I didn't notice the dawn;",fmt:"poem"},{zh:"处处闻啼鸟。",py:"Chùchù wén tí niǎo.",en:"Everywhere I hear the birds singing.",fmt:"poem"},{zh:"夜来风雨声，",py:"Yè lái fēng yǔ shēng,",en:"Last night came the sound of wind and rain;",fmt:"poem"},{zh:"花落知多少。",py:"Huā luò zhī duōshǎo.",en:"How many flowers have fallen, I wonder?",fmt:"poem"},{zh:"孟浩然（689—740）是唐代著名诗人。这首诗写的是春天的早晨刚醒来时的景色。",py:"Mèng Hàorán (689—740) shì Tángdài zhùmíng shīrén. Zhè shǒu shī xiě de shì chūntiān de zǎochen gāng xǐnglai shí de jǐngsè.",en:"Meng Haoran (689–740) was a famous poet of the Tang dynasty. This poem describes the scene on a spring morning just after waking up."},{zh:"在春天的晚上一直甜甜地睡到天亮，醒来听见鸟叫的声音，这时才想起昨夜好像下过雨、刮过风，不由得想：被风雨吹打下来的花儿不知道有多少啊。",py:"Zài chūntiān de wǎnshang yìzhí tiántián de shuìdào tiān liàng, xǐnglai tīngjiàn niǎo jiào de shēngyīn, zhè shí cái xiǎngqǐ zuóyè hǎoxiàng xiàguo yǔ, guāguo fēng, bùyóude xiǎng: bèi fēngyǔ chuīdǎ xialai de huār bù zhīdào yǒu duōshao a.",en:"On a spring night, the poet sleeps sweetly all the way until daybreak. Waking to the sound of birds singing, he only then remembers that there seemed to be rain and wind last night, and he can't help wondering: how many flowers have the wind and rain knocked down?"},{zh:"静夜思",py:"Jìng Yè Sī",en:"Quiet Night Thoughts",fmt:"h"},{zh:"李白",py:"Lǐ Bái",en:"Li Bai",fmt:"poem"},{zh:"床前明月光，",py:"Chuáng qián míng yuè guāng,",en:"Before my bed, the bright moonlight shines;",fmt:"poem"},{zh:"疑是地上霜。",py:"Yí shì dì shang shuāng.",en:"I wonder if it is frost upon the ground.",fmt:"poem"},{zh:"举头望明月，",py:"Jǔ tóu wàng míng yuè,",en:"I raise my head and gaze at the bright moon;",fmt:"poem"},{zh:"低头思故乡。",py:"Dī tóu sī gùxiāng.",en:"I lower my head and think of home.",fmt:"poem"},{zh:"李白（701—762）是中国古代最伟大的诗人之一。这首诗写的是诗人在静静的月夜想念故乡。",py:"Lǐ Bái (701—762) shì Zhōngguó gǔdài zuì wěidà de shīrén zhī yī. Zhè shǒu shī xiě de shì shīrén zài jìngjìng de yuèyè xiǎngniàn gùxiāng.",en:"Li Bai (701–762) was one of the greatest poets of ancient China. This poem is about the poet missing his hometown on a quiet moonlit night."},{zh:"坐在床前看着明月照在地上，好像白霜一样。诗人看到天空中的明月，不由得低下头来，想念自己的故乡。",py:"Zuò zài chuáng qián kànzhe míngyuè zhào zài dìshang, hǎoxiàng bái shuāng yíyàng. Shīrén kàndào tiānkōng zhōng de míngyuè, bùyóude dīxia tóu lai, xiǎngniàn zìjǐ de gùxiāng.",en:"Sitting before his bed, he watches the bright moon shining on the ground, which looks like white frost. Seeing the bright moon in the sky, the poet can't help lowering his head and missing his hometown."}],vocab:[],points:[],think:[],tf:[],mc:[],tip:null},{n:25,title:"绑在一起的翅膀",py:"Bǎng zài yìqǐ de chìbǎng",en:"Wings Tied Together",chars:362,daodu:"",daoduEn:"",paras:[{zh:"在森林里，住着两只鸟。一只住在东边，一只住在西边。有一天，东边的鸟在森林中间遇见了西边的鸟。因为它们第一次遇到和自己长得一样的鸟，所以很快成了好朋友。两只鸟每天早上都飞到森林中间见面，一起找食物，晚上再各自飞回自己的巢。它们觉得在一起的时间过得特别快。它们相爱了。",py:"Zài sēnlín li, zhùzhe liǎng zhī niǎo. Yì zhī zhù zài dōngbian, yì zhī zhù zài xībian. Yǒu yì tiān, dōngbian de niǎo zài sēnlín zhōngjiān yùjiànle xībian de niǎo. Yīnwèi tāmen dì-yī cì yùdào hé zìjǐ zhǎng de yíyàng de niǎo, suǒyǐ hěn kuài chéngle hǎo péngyou. Liǎng zhī niǎo měi tiān zǎoshang dōu fēidào sēnlín zhōngjiān jiànmiàn, yìqǐ zhǎo shíwù, wǎnshang zài gèzì fēihuí zìjǐ de cháo. Tāmen juéde zài yìqǐ de shíjiān guò de tèbié kuài. Tāmen xiāng'ài le.",en:"Two birds lived in a forest. One lived in the east, and the other lived in the west. One day, the bird from the east met the bird from the west in the middle of the forest. It was the first time either of them had met a bird that looked just like itself, so they soon became good friends. Every morning the two birds flew to the middle of the forest to meet and look for food together, and in the evening each flew back to its own nest. They felt that time together went by especially fast. They fell in love."},{zh:"为了可以一直在一起，很快它们就离开了自己的巢，一起在森林中间建了一个大巢。但是，两只鸟太相爱了，它们觉得这样还是不够，因为它们有时候在林间找食物时，还会看不到对方。“为了证明我们深深地相爱，我们把翅膀绑在一起吧。”一只鸟说。“好啊。”另一只鸟答应了。于是，它们用枝条把自己的翅膀绑在了一起。",py:"Wèile kěyǐ yìzhí zài yìqǐ, hěn kuài tāmen jiù líkāile zìjǐ de cháo, yìqǐ zài sēnlín zhōngjiān jiànle yí gè dà cháo. Dànshì, liǎng zhī niǎo tài xiāng'ài le, tāmen juéde zhèyàng háishi bú gòu, yīnwèi tāmen yǒu shíhou zài lín jiān zhǎo shíwù shí, hái huì kànbudào duìfāng. “Wèile zhèngmíng wǒmen shēnshēn de xiāng'ài, wǒmen bǎ chìbǎng bǎng zài yìqǐ ba.” Yì zhī niǎo shuō. “Hǎo a.” Lìng yì zhī niǎo dāying le. Yúshì, tāmen yòng zhītiáo bǎ zìjǐ de chìbǎng bǎng zàile yìqǐ.",en:`So that they could always be together, they soon left their own nests and built one big nest together in the middle of the forest. But the two birds were so much in love that they felt this still wasn't enough, because sometimes, when they were looking for food among the trees, they couldn't see each other. "To prove how deeply we love each other, let's tie our wings together," said one bird. "All right," the other bird agreed. So they tied their wings together with twigs.`},{zh:"第二天早上，两只鸟醒来后准备一起去找食物。但当它们跳出鸟巢时，却同时重重地摔在了地上。这时它们才知道，两只鸟虽然有四只翅膀，但绑在一起，却谁也不能飞。它们一起咬开枝条，张开翅膀飞向空中。一只鸟说：“爱，需要空间。”另一只鸟说：“爱，也需要自由。”",py:"Dì-èr tiān zǎoshang, liǎng zhī niǎo xǐnglai hòu zhǔnbèi yìqǐ qù zhǎo shíwù. Dàn dāng tāmen tiàochū niǎocháo shí, què tóngshí zhòngzhòng de shuāi zàile dìshang. Zhè shí tāmen cái zhīdào, liǎng zhī niǎo suīrán yǒu sì zhī chìbǎng, dàn bǎng zài yìqǐ, què shéi yě bù néng fēi. Tāmen yìqǐ yǎokāi zhītiáo, zhāngkāi chìbǎng fēixiàng kōngzhōng. Yì zhī niǎo shuō: “Ài, xūyào kōngjiān.” Lìng yì zhī niǎo shuō: “Ài, yě xūyào zìyóu.”",en:'The next morning, the two birds woke up and got ready to look for food together. But when they jumped out of the nest, they both fell hard to the ground at the same moment. Only then did they realize that although the two birds had four wings, tied together, neither of them could fly. Together they bit through the twigs, spread their wings and flew up into the sky. One bird said: "Love needs space." The other bird said: "Love also needs freedom."'},{zh:"两只鸟从此过着幸福快乐的日子。",py:"Liǎng zhī niǎo cóngcǐ guòzhe xìngfú kuàilè de rìzi.",en:"From then on, the two birds lived happily ever after."}],vocab:[],points:[],think:[],tf:[],mc:[],tip:null}],a={key:n,title:e,titleEn:h,series:i,seriesEn:t,level:o,lessons:s};export{a as default,n as key,s as lessons,o as level,i as series,t as seriesEn,e as title,h as titleEn};
